[2026-11-17T11:54:20.285Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'gh pr view 142 --repo konard/voice-simulator --json title,body,comments,reviews,statusCheckRollup,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,isDraft,url && gh api repos/konard/voice-simulator/pulls/142/comments --paginate && gh api repos/konard/voice-simulator/pulls/142/reviews --paginate && gh api repos/konard/voice-simulator/issues/142/comments --paginate'","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"body\":\"Add an experimental syllable-nucleus, acoustic-landmark and eight-class detector, with batch/stream APIs, public types, deterministic calibration, a JSON CLI command and matching Rust/WASM numerics.\\n\\nFixes #62\\n\\n**Unfinished: the three required quality gates remain failing. Keep this PR draft and unmerged until every acceptance criterion passes.** The [requirement inventory and reproductions](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/docs/case-studies/issue-62/README.md) distinguish implemented mechanics from unmet criteria. There are no required sub-issues; prerequisites #58 and #17 are closed. No quality assertion or CI gate has been weakened.\\n\\nThe implementation includes:\\n\\n- Mel sonority, voiced peak confirmation, coarse/fine band landmarks, the specified fixed class tree and temporal cleanup. The irreversible streaming rules have the unresolved contradictions described below.\\n- Full deterministic calibration of 3780 clean/noisy recordings, three rounds of 21-value coordinate search, generated recall comments, CLI help, documentation, roadmap and a minor changeset.\\n- A streaming suppression regression and fix: the old detector emitted two `b-` events 5 ms apart while batch mode kept one. It now preserves earlier suppression decisions and neighbouring band context. The regression covers both hops, four chunk sizes, nonzero start time, immutable appended events, strengths, batch equality and same-type separation.\\n- An anatomy-download cancellation fix exposed by CI. Cancellation reaches requests, bodies and retry waits; live fixture preparation has a 20-second total budget before test registration. Transport failures print explicit skip diagnostics; corrupt archives and programming errors fail. Seven mocked regressions pass on all runtimes; two fail before the fix.\\n- The latest `main`, `eeb2869` (PR #147), merged with history preserved. Retain every existing acoustic, formant, inverse-filter, codebook, IPA-recognition, language-identification and mixed-decoding API/type, CLI command and parity suite, together with landmark parity in the Rust job.\\n\\nThe merged scalar WASM measures **467028 bytes**, SHA-256 `dedd72fab32a042aeed066d322c6b3ec0b98fe3c5437f9801a5f490b35e0b4ee`. The build and size regression enforce the next 16 KiB budget, **475136 bytes**. SIMD is 473723 bytes and remains unshipped. Both landmark and language-identification WASM modules are retained.\\n\\nReproduction and validation:\\n\\n```sh\\n# Required quality suite: 9 pass, 3 fail.\\nnode --max-old-space-size=256 --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/recognition-landmarks.test.js\\n\\n# Focused merged engine: 73 pass, no skips.\\nCARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1 node scripts/build-wasm.mjs --require\\nREQUIRE_WASM=1 node --max-old-space-size=256 --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-timeout=30000 tests/engine-parity.test.js tests/engine-features.test.js tests/rust-landmarks.test.js tests/rust-recognition.test.js tests/rust-inverse-filter.test.js tests/engine-size.test.js tests/recognition-landmark-streaming.test.js\\nnpm run check\\ncargo fmt --all -- --check\\n\\n# Independent finite counterexamples and candidate bounds.\\nnode --max-old-space-size=128 experiments/issue-62/edge-feasibility.mjs\\nnode --max-old-space-size=128 experiments/issue-62/stream-closure.mjs\\nnode --max-old-space-size=256 experiments/issue-62/nucleus-ceiling.mjs --smoothing-sensitivity\\nnode --max-old-space-size=64 experiments/issue-62/confirmation.mjs\\n```\\n\\nThe focused merged-engine checks, repository checks and Rust formatting pass. After the latest merge, both the independent edge probe and public PCM counterexample produce byte-identical output on Node.js, Bun (`--smol`) and Deno (`--v8-flags=--max-old-space-size=128`). Logs use the local `ci-logs/restart-5-main-eeb2869-` prefix. Earlier full calibrations wrote byte-identical formatted files twice (SHA-256 `01e01bce0d21594143f2fef34dcda058430a1cac740526f2e7f9fb45356b1203`); tenth-material stability passed. The [24-utterance golden report](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/docs/case-studies/issue-62/golden-report.md) measures MARE 24.41%; 15% is a target, not a gate.\\n\\nCurrent-commit CI:\\n\\n[Run 44071097877](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44071097877) ran **11:07:18–11:24:57 UTC on 2026-11-17**, checking merge commit `190bde281044e5bf2abd3c7907ae180a88872cb5` after its 11:06:49 UTC commit. **Every workflow and job has finished.** All nine runtime jobs failed exactly the three quality assertions below; Pipeline Status correctly fails because of those jobs. All other applicable checks passed, including Rust, compilation, lint, simulation, documentation, release preflight, Docker, security, workflow tooling, link checks and the example app. Node/Ubuntu: **2968 pass, 134 skip, 3 fail**, none cancelled. Rust: **112 workspace, 187 parity and 7 threaded-engine tests pass**. CI reproduces the scalar WASM size and hash above exactly. Latest `main` (`eeb2869`) is an ancestor, the remote PR head matches, and the working tree is clean.\\n\\nRTF was **0.000125–0.001187**, below 0.02 everywhere. Bun/macOS finished in 456 seconds of its existing 500-second test budget, Bun/Windows in 387 seconds, and Bun/Ubuntu in 208 seconds. No test or suite timed out. The complete log is preserved locally as `ci-logs/checks-44071097877.log` (**52041 lines**). Node/Ubuntu measurements are at **13121–13129**, and error details at **15136, 15148 and 15162**, pointing to `tests/recognition-landmarks.test.js:174`, `:247` and `:280`. Error blocks from every failing runtime job were inspected. Previous [run 44067794069](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44067794069) on `855b325` has the same three failures; its complete log and earlier matching SHAs/timestamps are also preserved.\\n\\n| Unmet check | Measured | Required |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Nuclei | 63.3333% recall; 33.3333% extras/truth | At least 90%; at most 10% |\\n| Classes, 16 / 8 kHz | 48.2459% / 47.1143% accuracy | At least 85% / 80% |\\n| Edges | Missing `apa` g−/g+ at 0.174/0.260 s and `ama` s−/s+ at 0.178/0.230 s | Each within 20 ms |\\n\\nThe blockers are supported by independent, bounded reproductions:\\n\\n- **Nucleus candidate ceiling:** even every permitted voiced local maximum, before noise/dip/spacing rejection, covers only **98/120 centres (81.67%)** within 50 ms. This optimistic bound allows one candidate to cover multiple centres. Alternative common 40 ms moving means cover 94, 93 and 96 centres. Threshold tuning cannot reach 90% on the required signals under the prescribed candidate rule.\\n- **Fine-peak placement:** the [independent edge probe](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/experiments/issue-62/edge-feasibility.mjs) reads public band-0 frames, without calling the detector or requiring coarse peaks, strength, voicing crossings or suppression. No falling fine peak is within 20 ms of the `apa` closure at **0.17407036 s**. Nearest errors are 25.930 ms with 15 ms rounding, 20.930 ms with 10 ms rounding, 25.930 ms with literal 13 ms interpolation on the frame grid, and 23.930 ms with continuous interpolation over every slope change. No threshold/grouping change supplies this edge at a required fine peak on these signals. The bound does not cover the other missing edges.\\n- **Immutable classes versus retrospective closure:** the [public PCM reproduction](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/experiments/issue-62/stream-closure.mjs) supplies two signals identical through 0.4325 s, including analyzer lookahead. For the frame at 0.360 s, the 60 ms commitment deadline is 0.420 s. Speech returns at 0.440 or 0.600 s; final cleanup requires closure in one case and silence in the other. A causal detector must give the same answer at the deadline. The draft preserves committed silence in both cases and cannot implement the first signal's retrospective closure.\\n- **Irrevocable nuclei versus later replacement:** identical sonority prefixes require confirmation of a peak after its dip and 40 ms maximum window, before a higher peak 60 ms later that must replace it under the 80 ms rule. Both requirements cannot hold together.\\n\\nThese criteria need consistent signal/detection, timing-reference and streaming-commitment rules before they can all be implemented. Class accuracy remains independently unresolved: the diagnostic sentence-label search reaches only 70.9166%/69.7473%, establishes no global bound and is not used to fit shipped thresholds to the test sentences. Passing counterexample assertions validate the evidence; they do not satisfy the detector's acceptance criteria.\\n\\nManual release setup on `main`:\\n\\nLatest default-branch [run 44069345575](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44069345575) on `eeb2869e1e91f3390120269287a0fc19771232c3` passes all nine runtime jobs and Rust checks but fails Release Preflight and Pipeline Status because npm has no published package or bootstrap token. Its complete log is preserved as `ci-logs/main-checks-44069345575.log` (48225 lines); lines **152–160** state the action. Earlier main run 44060989726 has the same error. The existing workflow skips only the credential-dependent operation with an explanation on PRs and fails explicitly on `main`.\\n\\nA maintainer must add repository Actions secret **`NPM_TOKEN` containing a granular token allowed to publish `voice-simulator`** at [Actions secrets](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/settings/secrets/actions), then rerun the release. After first publication, configure the trusted publisher for repository `konard/voice-simulator`, workflow `release.yml`, at [npm package access](https://www.npmjs.com/package/voice-simulator/access), then delete the bootstrap secret. This account action is separate from the PR's three quality failures.\\n\",\"comments\":[{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVMlws88AAAABnb5ckQ\",\"author\":{\"login\":\"konard\"},\"authorAssociation\":\"OWNER\",\"body\":\"<!-- hive-mind:working-session-summary -->\\n## Working session summary\\n\\nUpdated [PR #142](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142), but it remains **draft and unfinished**.\\n\\nImplementation, regression tests, calibration, and Rust parity are committed. Lint, formatting, Rust checks, and four CI workflows pass. Three quality gates still fail:\\n\\n- Nucleus recall: 63.33%, below 90%.\\n- Class accuracy: 48.25% / 47.11%, below 85% / 80%.\\n- Four required landmark edges remain missing or outside tolerance.\\n\\nReproducible experiments expose conflicting requirements: permitted nucleus candidates cover at most 81.67% of reference centres, and retrospective silence relabeling conflicts with immutable labels after 60 ms. Confirmed-peak replacement also remains unresolved.\\n\\nThe PR documents every remaining criterion, reproduction commands, and CI evidence. No failing tests were disabled. The working tree is clean, latest `main` is included, and the PR remains unmerged.\\n\\n---\\n*This summary was automatically extracted from the AI working session output.*\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-17T07:16:58Z\",\"includesCreatedEdit\":false,\"isMinimized\":false,\"minimizedReason\":\"\",\"reactionGroups\":[],\"url\":\"https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6941465745\",\"viewerDidAuthor\":true},{\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVM