es. Signals and all feature prefixes are identical at\n      the commitment deadline, including front-end window lookahead.\n- [x] Run the focused Node suite: 9 pass, 3 unchanged quality failures.\n- [x] Validate, commit and push the public-API counterexample and updated\n      evidence in a6e3e83; review its final diff and clean working tree.\n- [x] Inspect all a6e3e83 CI results and preserve the complete failure log.\n      All nine jobs have the same three quality failures; other checks pass.\n- [x] Merge newly advanced main 80b9c3d, retaining the feature inventory,\n      engine parity and landmark parity suites. Measure combined WASM:\n      scalar 415183, SIMD 421828 (unshipped), next 16 KiB budget 425984.\n- [x] Verify the merged engine: 70 focused checks pass without skips;\n      cargo fmt passes. The public PCM conflict repeats on all runtimes,\n      and the focused quality suite retains the same three failures.\n- [x] Commit and push the merge, inspect all resulting CI and update\n      PR 142 with the final evidence.\n- [ ] Complete all original quality and timing requirements. Blocked by\n      the unchanged incompatible contract; class and edge accuracy also\n      remain unresolved. No test waiver is authorised by this finding.\n- [ ] Mark ready only after all requirements and all CI checks pass.\n\n## Fifth restart: independently bound the fine-band edge candidates\n\n- [x] Re-read the complete issue, all comments and reviews; required\n      sub-issues remain empty and prerequisites remain closed.\n- [x] Fetch origin and confirm main 80b9c3d is already in HEAD 311681b.\n- [x] Download latest failed run 44062832031 and default-branch run\n      44060989726, verify SHAs/timestamps, and inspect actual failures.\n- [x] Reproduce the focused quality suite: nine pass, three fail, with\n      unchanged nucleus, class and edge measurements.\n- [x] Change approach: independently enumerate the necessary fine-band\n      falling peaks through the public analyzer, without calling the\n      detector or any of its numerical helpers. Check rounding both ways,\n      literal 13 ms interpolation and all continuous-time slope changes.\n      No allowed peak is within 20 ms of the requested apa closure edge.\n- [x] Recheck nucleus smoothing sensitivity and class-search diagnostics.\n      Neither provides a valid route to the required quality gates.\n- [x] Verify the new finite experiment on Node.js, Bun and Deno; check\n      formatting/lint and commit the experiment and exact evidence.\n- [ ] Push only issue-62-c339234ca063, review the current diff, update\n      PR 142 and wait for every resulting CI job to finish.\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria pass. Blocked by the unchanged nucleus,\n      fine-peak placement and causal commitment contradictions. Class\n      accuracy also remains unresolved; do not waive its gate.\n- [ ] Mark ready only after every requirement and all checks pass.\n\n### New main during the fifth-restart CI\n\n- [x] Wait for every 855b325 workflow, preserve full run 44067794069 and\n      inspect all nine runtime error blocks. Only the same three quality\n      assertions fail; all other applicable checks pass.\n- [x] Fetch newly advanced main eeb2869 and resolve both WASM modules and\n      the measured size-budget conflicts, retaining all APIs and suites.\n      Combined scalar is 467028 bytes, SIMD 473723 (unshipped), next\n      16 KiB budget 475136. Build with CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=1.\n- [x] Verify the merged build with focused parity, check the unchanged\n      quality failures and feasibility probes, and run formatting/lint.\n- [ ] Commit and push the merge, review its diff, inspect all resulting\n      CI and update the PR with final measurements and blockers.\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:171:The intonation of [#51](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/51) (`src/articulation/intonation.js`) splits every intonation phrase into pre-nucleus, nucleus and tail and puts the pitch at `register + declination + range * tune` semitones, with the targets of `TUNES` per language approached at `INTONATION_RATE` = 60: English statement, yes/no, wh, alternative, tag, echo, continuation, list and exclamation tunes; the Russian constructions IK1 to IK7 (IK3 for yes/no questions, IK2 with the centre on the wh-word, IK4 for short `а`-questions and IK5 for `какой … !`, both detected in g2p and written as `{IK4 … IK4}`); Hindi accent phrases (every word of two or more syllables before the last word, low on its first vowel and high on its last, each one 1 st lower; a sketch not yet fitted to recordings); and for Mandarin a raise that grows to +3 st over a question without a particle (+1 after 吗, none with a wh-word), so tones are never replaced. Focus (`*word*`, `<emphasis>`, `ˈˈ`, `FOCUS`) raises the nucleus by 2.9 st, lengthens it 1.2× and adds 3 dB, and compresses what follows. g2p writes `↘ ?`, `↗ ?`, `↗ |` before `or`/`или`, and a `|` break with a continuation in stretches over 14 syllables; `|` is a continuation (Russian IK3 × 0.7), and the tune names can be set by `[tune name]`, `<vs:tune name=\"…\">` or the IPA marks, which win over the punctuation ([docs/markup.md](markup.md#intonation)). Measured with a 150 Hz head (`node experiments/issue-51-measure.mjs`, [experiments/issue-51-measure.txt](../experiments/issue-51-measure.txt), 23/23 pass): `You are coming.` falls 5.13 st, `Are you coming?` rises 7.71 st from the nucleus, `Tea or coffee?` (`ˈti ↗ | ˈɔɹ ˈkɑfi ↘ ?`) rises 5.83 st on `tea` and ends 10.99 st below it, the IK3 centre of `Это мама?` rises 8.82 st, `你来？` is 2.59 st above `你来。` on the last syllable while 去 still falls 4.46 st, and the focused `Anna` peaks 3.10 st higher. In [experiments/issue-11-audit.txt](../experiments/issue-11-audit.txt) the last f0 of `Tea or coffee?` went from 143 to 84 Hz and that of `You are coming.` from 95 to 90 Hz; in [experiments/issue-11-audit-m3b.txt](../experiments/issue-11-audit-m3b.txt) the mean of `你来？` went from 119 to 135 Hz, against 119 for `你来。`.\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:220:The draft implementation of [#62](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/62)\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:222:mel sonority, two-scale band landmarks and a calibrated fixed class tree.\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:224:98/120 synthetic reference nuclei (81.67%), below the 90% gate, and deciding\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:244:| [#62](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/62) | Feature | Syllable nuclei, landmarks and broad sound classes                             | [#58](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/58), [#17](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/17)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | R6, R10, R12, R13, R18          |\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:248:| [#66](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/66) | Feature | Decode articulation into IPA with times                                        | [#65](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/65), [#62](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/62)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | R6, R7, R10, R12, R13, R18, R19 |\ndocs/ROADMAP.md:341:    P50[\"#62\"]\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:7:import { calibrationMaterial } from '../../scripts/landmark-material.mjs';\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:11:} from '../../scripts/calibrate-landmarks.mjs';\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:12:import { LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS } from '../../src/recognition/landmark-thresholds.js';\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:14:describe('recognition landmarks: golden set', () => {\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:23:        ).nuclei.length;\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:35:      'recognition-landmarks',\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:37:        '# Syllable nuclei on the golden set (issue 62)',\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:39:        'Command: `node --test tests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js`.',\ntests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js:43:        '| Utterance | True syllables | Found nuclei | Absolute relative error |',\nbin/voice-simulator.js:128:    '  landmarks <file>    Syllable nuclei, sound changes and broad classes',\nbin/voice-simulator.js:843:  landmarks(values, positionals, io) {\nREADME.md:68:  (`*word*`) moves the nucleus; a tune can be named (`[tune IK4]…[/tune]`,\nREADME.md:1491:Experimental syllable nuclei and sound classes: `findLandmarks`, `createLandmarkDetector` and `BROAD_CLASSES`. See the [API and measured limits](docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md); issue #62 remains unfinished.\n-rw-r--r-- 1 box box 15861 Nov 17 11:53 src/engine/wasm-loader.js\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
