[2026-11-17T11:56:19.649Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md && cat tests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js && cat tests/rust-landmarks.test.js && cat scripts/landmark-material.mjs'","aggregated_output":"# Experimental syllable nuclei and acoustic landmarks\n\n`findLandmarks(frames, options)` reads the analysis front end's mel energies,\nperiodicity and six frequency bands. It returns `hop`, `startTime`, `count`,\n`committed`, `classes` (`Uint8Array`), `sonority` (`Float32Array`), `nuclei`\n(`time`, `start`, `end`, `strength`) and `landmarks` (`time`, `type`, `strength`).\nThe arrays have `frames.capacity` entries, with `count` valid rows.\n`BROAD_CLASSES` lists class names in numerical order: silence, vowel, glide,\nnasal, voiced fricative, voiceless fricative, closure and burst. Landmark\nsigns `g`, `s` and `b` mark voicing, sonorant and burst/frication changes.\nTimes and the hop are seconds; strengths are dB.\n\n```js\nimport {\n  createFrameAnalyzer,\n  createLandmarkDetector,\n  findLandmarks,\n} from 'voice-simulator';\n\nconst analyzer = createFrameAnalyzer(16000);\nconst detector = createLandmarkDetector(analyzer.frames);\nanalyzer.push(chunk);\nconst newlyConfirmedNuclei = detector.advance();\nanalyzer.flush();\ndetector.advance(true); // drain at the end of the recording\nconst batch = findLandmarks(analyzer.frames);\n```\n\n`options.thresholds` overrides the documented tree's numeric thresholds.\nStreaming arrays before `committed` remain fixed. Detections are appended;\nnucleus boundaries are completed as following minima arrive. Recreate a\nstage after trimming or resetting the analyzer. The command\n`voice-simulator landmarks recording.wav` writes the same result as JSON;\n`-o landmarks.json` saves it to a file.\n\nWhen a following peak reveals a deeper boundary minimum, both `end` and\n`strength` are updated. Strength remains the peak sonority minus the lower\nsonority at the two reported boundaries.\n\nThese APIs are experimental. The prescribed voiced local maxima cover only\n98 of 120 synthetic reference centres (81.67%, before any detection filters),\nbelow issue 62's 90% requirement. Also, deciding whether a silence run is\nshorter than 150 ms requires more future sound than the requested 60 ms\ncommitment deadline. Irrevocable early nucleus confirmation also conflicts\nwith replacing a lower peak when a higher one follows within 80 ms.\nBatch clean-up relabels such bounded runs as closure;\na stream preserves committed labels. Reproductions and remaining acceptance\ncriteria are in [the issue 62 investigation](case-studies/issue-62/README.md).\nRun `node scripts/calibrate-landmarks.mjs` to regenerate thresholds and\n`npm run test:heavy -- --suite recognition` for calibration stability and\nsyllable counts on the golden recordings. No accuracy target is claimed met.\n/** Golden-set syllable counts and the complete threshold recalibration.\n * Run with npm run test:heavy -- --suite recognition. */\nimport { describe, it, expect } from 'test-anywhere';\nimport { analyzeFrames, findLandmarks, syllabifyIpa } from '../../src/index.js';\nimport { loadGolden, isReviewed } from '../helpers/golden.js';\nimport { heavyLimit, writeReport } from './helpers/report.js';\nimport { calibrationMaterial } from '../../scripts/landmark-material.mjs';\nimport {\n  calibrate,\n  SEARCH_RANGES,\n} from '../../scripts/calibrate-landmarks.mjs';\nimport { LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS } from '../../src/recognition/landmark-thresholds.js';\n\ndescribe('recognition landmarks: golden set', () => {\n  it('counts syllables per utterance and writes the report', () => {\n    const rows = loadGolden()\n      .slice(0, heavyLimit(Infinity))\n      .map((item) => {\n        const truth = syllabifyIpa(item.ipa, { language: item.lang }).flat()\n          .length;\n        const found = findLandmarks(\n          analyzeFrames(item.samples, item.sampleRate)\n        ).nuclei.length;\n        return {\n          id: item.id,\n          reviewed: isReviewed(item),\n          true: truth,\n          found,\n          relativeError: Math.abs(found - truth) / truth,\n        };\n      });\n    const meanAbsoluteRelativeError =\n      rows.reduce((sum, row) => sum + row.relativeError, 0) / rows.length;\n    writeReport(\n      'recognition-landmarks',\n      [\n        '# Syllable nuclei on the golden set (issue 62)',\n        '',\n        'Command: `node --test tests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js`.',\n        'Truth: syllabifyIpa of the committed IPA, by language. An asterisk',\n        'marks an utterance whose text and IPA have not both been reviewed by a person.',\n        '',\n        '| Utterance | True syllables | Found nuclei | Absolute relative error |',\n        '| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |',\n        ...rows.map(\n          (r) =>\n            `| ${r.id}${r.reviewed ? '' : '*'} | ${r.true} | ${r.found} | ${(100 * r.relativeError).toFixed(2)}% |`\n        ),\n        '',\n        `Mean absolute relative error: **${(100 * meanAbsoluteRelativeError).toFixed(2)}%**.`,\n        'The 15% target is measured, not a gate.',\n        '',\n      ].join('\\n'),\n      { rows, meanAbsoluteRelativeError }\n    );\n    expect(rows.length > 0).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it('thresholds are up to date', () => {\n    const result = calibrate(calibrationMaterial(0.1));\n    for (const [key, [low, high]] of Object.entries(SEARCH_RANGES)) {\n      const difference = Math.abs(\n        result.thresholds[key] - LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS[key]\n      );\n      console.log(\n        `threshold ${key}: tenth ${result.thresholds[key]}, committed ${LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS[key]}, difference ${difference}`\n      );\n      expect(difference <= (high - low) / 20 + 1e-8).toBe(true);\n    }\n  });\n});\n/** Class B numerical parity of the complete landmark detector. The Rust\n * stage reads the same frame set, not separately recomputed spectra. */\nimport { describe, expect } from 'test-anywhere';\nimport {\n  analyzeFrames,\n  findLandmarks,\n  presetHeadConfig,\n  synthesize,\n} from '../src/index.js';\nimport { LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS } from '../src/recognition/landmark-thresholds.js';\nimport { float64View } from '../src/engine/wasm-loader.js';\nimport { loadRustEngine, noRust } from './helpers/rust-engine.js';\nimport { itUnless } from './helpers/skip.js';\nimport { boundaryFrames } from './helpers/landmark-frames.js';\nconst it = itUnless(noRust);\nconst KEYS = [\n  'silence',\n  'voiced',\n  'fricativeZcr',\n  'fricativeGravity',\n  'nasalDrop',\n  'nasalBelowPeak',\n  'glideBelowPeak',\n  'nucleusAboveNoise',\n  'nucleusDip',\n  'landmarkRise',\n];\nconst TYPES = ['b+', 'b-', 'g+', 'g-', 's+', 's-'];\nfunction packedFrames(frames) {\n  const rows = new Float64Array(frames.count * (13 + frames.melBands));\n  for (let t = 0; t < frames.count; t++) {\n    const row = t * (13 + frames.melBands);\n    for (const [k, key] of [\n      'energy',\n      'noise',\n      'speech',\n      'periodicity',\n      'zcr',\n      'gravity',\n      'tilt',\n    ].entries()) {\n      rows[row + k] = frames[key][t];\n    }\n    rows.set(frames.band.subarray(t * 6, t * 6 + 6), row + 7);\n    rows.set(\n      frames.mel.subarray(t * frames.melBands, (t + 1) * frames.melBands),\n      row + 13\n    );\n  }\n  return rows;\n}\nasync function rustResult(frames) {\n  const engine = await loadRustEngine();\n  const rows = packedFrames(frames);\n  const sizes = [rows.byteLength, 80, frames.count * 12 * 8];\n  const pointers = sizes.map((n) => engine.exports.vs_alloc(Math.max(8, n)));\n  try {\n    float64View(engine, pointers[0], rows.length).set(rows);\n    float64View(engine, pointers[1], 10).set(\n      KEYS.map((key) => LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS[key])\n    );\n    expect(\n      engine.exports.vs_landmarks(\n        pointers[0],\n        frames.count,\n        frames.melBands,\n        frames.rate,\n        frames.hop,\n        pointers[1],\n        pointers[2]\n      )\n    ).toBe(0);\n    return float64View(engine, pointers[2], frames.count * 12).slice();\n  } finally {\n    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n      engine.exports.vs_free(pointers[i], Math.max(8, sizes[i]));\n    }\n  }\n}\nfunction packedExpected(result) {\n  const rows = new Float64Array(result.count * 12);\n  for (let t = 0; t < result.count; t++) {\n    rows[t * 12] = result.classes[t];\n    rows[t * 12 + 1] = result.sonority[t];\n  }\n  for (const nucleus of result.nuclei) {\n    const row = Math.round((nucleus.time - result.startTime) / result.hop) * 12;\n    rows[row + 2] = 1;\n    rows[row + 3] = (nucleus.start - result.startTime) / result.hop;\n    rows[row + 4] =\n      nucleus.end === null ? -1 : (nucleus.end - result.startTime) / result.hop;\n    rows[row + 5] = nucleus.strength;\n  }\n  for (const landmark of result.landmarks) {\n    rows[\n      Math.round((landmark.time - result.startTime) / result.hop) * 12 +\n        6 +\n        TYPES.indexOf(landmark.type)\n    ] = landmark.strength;\n  }\n  return rows;\n}\ndescribe('Rust landmark parity', () => {\n  it('matches strengths after a deeper boundary replaces an early minimum', async () => {\n    for (const trailingSilence of [false, true]) {\n      const frames = boundaryFrames(trailingSilence);\n      const expected = packedExpected(findLandmarks(frames));\n      const actual = await rustResult(frames);\n      for (let i = 0; i < expected.length; i++) {\n        expect(Math.abs(actual[i] - expected[i]) <= 1e-6).toBe(true);\n      }\n    }\n  });\n  it('matches the JavaScript sonority, classes, nuclei and landmarks', async () => {\n    for (const rate of [8000, 11025, 16000]) {\n      for (const preset of ['male', 'female']) {\n        for (const hop of [0.005, 0.01]) {\n          const out = synthesize('apa asa ama aba', {\n            ipa: true,\n            head: presetHeadConfig(preset),\n            solver: 'waveguide',\n            engine: 'js',\n            sampleRate: rate,\n            seed: 1,\n          });\n          const frames = analyzeFrames(out.samples, rate, { hop });\n          const expected = packedExpected(findLandmarks(frames));\n          const actual = await rustResult(frames);\n          let error = 0,\n            power = 0;\n          for (let i = 0; i < expected.length; i++) {\n            error += (actual[i] - expected[i]) ** 2;\n            power += expected[i] ** 2;\n            if (i % 12 === 0 || i % 12 === 2) {\n              expect(actual[i]).toBe(expected[i]);\n            }\n          }\n          console.log(\n            `landmarks Rust ${preset}@${rate}/${hop}: relative RMS ${Math.sqrt(error / power)}`\n          );\n          expect(Math.sqrt(error / power) <= 1e-6).toBe(true);\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  });\n});\n/** Shared labelled material for calibration and independent accuracy tests.\n * Segment edges are excluded by 10 ms, as specified in issue 62. */\nimport { synthesize, presetHeadConfig, analyzeFrames } from '../src/index.js';\nimport { CONSONANTS } from '../src/ipa/inventory.js';\nimport { createRandom } from '../src/random.js';\nimport {\n  sonorityFilters,\n  fillSonority,\n  smoothSonority,\n} from '../src/recognition/landmark-signals.js';\n\nexport function segmentClass(segment, previous) {\n  if (segment.kind === 'pause') {\n    return 0;\n  }\n  if (segment.kind === 'vowel') {\n    return 1;\n  }\n  if (segment.kind === 'release') {\n    return 7;\n  }\n  return consonantClass(segment, previous);\n}\n\nfunction consonantClass(segment, previous) {\n  // The planner represents an affricate as two consonant segments sharing\n  // one token: [REDACTED] stop closure, then its voiced or unvoiced frication.\n  if (segment.token?.affricate) {\n    return previous?.token =[REDACTED] segment.token\n      ? segment.token.voiced\n        ? 4\n        : 5\n      : 6;\n  }\n  const manner = segment.token?.phoneme?.manner;\n  if (manner === 'plosive' || manner === 'click') {\n    return 6;\n  }\n  if (manner === 'nasal') {\n    return 3;\n  }\n  if (manner === 'fricative' || manner === 'lateral-fricative') {\n    return segment.token.voiced ? 4 : 5;\n  }\n  return 2;\n}\n\nexport function frameTruth(plan, frames) {\n  const truth = new Int8Array(frames.count).fill(-1);\n  for (let t = 0, i = 0; t < frames.count; t++) {\n    const time = frames.startTime + t * frames.hop;\n    while (i + 1 < plan.segments.length && plan.segments[i].end <= time) {\n      i++;\n    }\n    const seg = plan.segments[i];\n    if (time >= seg.start + 0.01 && time <= seg.end - 0.01) {\n      truth[t] = segmentClass(seg, plan.segments[i - 1]);\n    }\n  }\n  return truth;\n}\n\nexport function sonorityOf(frames) {\n  const raw = new Float32Array(frames.count);\n  const s = new Float32Array(frames.count);\n  fillSonority(frames, raw, 0, sonorityFilters(frames));\n  smoothSonority(raw, s, 0, frames.count, frames.hop);\n  return s;\n}\n\nexport function peakCurve(s, hop) {\n  const peak = new Float32Array(s.length);\n  for (let t = 0; t < s.length; t++) {\n    let max = -Infinity;\n    for (\n      let j = Math.max(0, t - Math.round(0.2 / hop));\n      j <= Math.min(s.length - 1, t + Math.round(0.04 / hop));\n      j++\n    ) {\n      max = Math.max(max, s[j]);\n    }\n    peak[t] = max;\n  }\n  return peak;\n}\n\n/** Deterministic striding samples vowels, rates and voices evenly,\n * retaining both the clean and noisy rendition of each selected item. */\nexport function calibrationMaterial(fraction = 1) {\n  if (!(fraction > 0 && fraction <= 1)) {\n    throw new RangeError('fraction must be in (0,1]');\n  }\n  const stride = Math.round(1 / fraction);\n  const material = [];\n  let index = 0;\n  for (const phone of Object.keys(CONSONANTS)) {\n    for (const vowel of ['a', 'i', 'u']) {\n      for (const preset of ['male', 'female', 'child']) {\n        for (const rate of [8000, 11025, 16000]) {\n          if (index++ % stride !== 0) {\n            continue;\n          }\n          material.push(...renderPair(phone, vowel, preset, rate));\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return material;\n}\n\nfunction renderPair(phone, vowel, preset, rate) {\n  const material = [];\n  const out = synthesize(`${vowel}${phone}${vowel}`, {\n    ipa: true,\n    head: presetHeadConfig(preset),\n    solver: 'waveguide',\n    engine: 'js',\n    sampleRate: rate,\n    seed: 1,\n  });\n  let power = 0;\n  for (const sample of out.samples) {\n    power += sample * sample;\n  }\n  const noiseAmplitude = Math.sqrt((3 * power) / out.samples.length / 100);\n  for (let noisy = 0; noisy < 2; noisy++) {\n    const random = createRandom(\n      `landmarks:${phone}:${vowel}:${preset}:${rate}`\n    );\n    const samples = noisy\n      ? Float32Array.from(\n          out.samples,\n          (x) => x + noiseAmplitude * (2 * random() - 1)\n        )\n      : out.samples;\n    const original = analyzeFrames(samples, rate);\n    const frames = {\n      rate,\n      hop: original.hop,\n      count: original.count,\n      capacity: original.count,\n      startTime: 0,\n      melBands: original.melBands,\n    };\n    for (const key of [\n      'energy',\n      'noise',\n      'speech',\n      'periodicity',\n      'zcr',\n      'gravity',\n      'tilt',\n      'band',\n    ]) {\n      frames[key] = original[key].slice(\n        0,\n        original.count * (key === 'band' ? 6 : 1)\n      );\n    }\n    const sonority = sonorityOf(original);\n    material.push({\n      id: `${vowel}${phone}${vowel}:${preset}:${rate}:${noisy}`,\n      frames,\n      sonority,\n      peak: peakCurve(sonority, frames.hop),\n      truth: frameTruth(out.plan, frames),\n    });\n  }\n  return material;\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
