[2026-11-17T11:56:30.390Z] [STDERR] # Roadmap
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.397Z] [STDERR] This is the step-by-step plan that takes voice-simulator from what it is today
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.400Z] [STDERR] to the [vision](VISION.md): a physical model of the human voice that speaks and
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.403Z] [STDERR] listens, without neural networks, in the public domain.
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.406Z] [STDERR] Every step is a GitHub issue. Every issue is marked as a **Bug** or a
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.409Z] [STDERR] **Feature**, belongs to one milestone, and names the issues that block it. The
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.412Z] [STDERR] issues were planned in
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.415Z] [STDERR] [issue 11](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/11); the analysis
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.421Z] [STDERR] behind them is the
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.425Z] [STDERR] [issue 11 case study](case-studies/issue-11/README.md).
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.432Z] [STDERR] ## How to use the roadmap
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.435Z] [STDERR] 1. Pick an open issue from the tables below whose "Blocked by" issues are all
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.439Z] [STDERR]    closed. Inside a milestone, take bugs before features.
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.441Z] [STDERR] 2. Read the issue from top to bottom. Each one has the same sections: Goal,
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.444Z] [STDERR]    Why, Current state, What to do, Tests, Acceptance criteria, Out of scope and
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.449Z] [STDERR]    References. The issue names the files, the functions and the numbers, so no
[2026-11-17T11:56:30.455Z] [STDERR]    other document is needed to start.
