[2026-11-17T11:57:04.920Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '500,560p' docs/ROADMAP.md && sed -n '220,235p' docs/ROADMAP.md && cat experiments/issue-62/stream-closure.mjs && cat tests/recognition-landmark-boundaries.test.js && git diff origin/main --stat\"","aggregated_output":"  public domain or CC0; anything else is downloaded at test time and never\n  committed.\n- One pull request per issue. Do not start before every issue under \"Blocked\n  by\" is closed.\n- Work in the JavaScript reference implementation in `src/` unless the issue\n  says otherwise. If the directory `crates/` exists when you start, implement\n  the same numerical code in the Rust core too and extend the parity tests,\n  following the interface rules, the determinism rules and the parity classes\n  of [RUST-ENGINE.md](RUST-ENGINE.md).\n- Same input, seed and options must give the same samples on Node.js, Bun and\n  Deno. Take randomness only from `src/random.js`.\n- Add tests in `tests/` that fail before the change and pass after it. Tests\n  that need more than about 10 seconds or a download run only in the manually\n  triggered workflow.\n- Keep every source and Markdown file under 1500 lines, run `npm run check` and\n  `npm test`, and add a changeset (`npm run changeset`) when code changes.\n- Update `README.md`, `src/index.d.ts`, the command line help and this file\n  when behaviour or the public API changes. Put experiment scripts in\n  `experiments/` and name them after the issue's number.\n- Report measured numbers with the command that produced them. Do not write a\n  claim that was not measured.\n\n## How the roadmap is maintained\n\n- The text of every issue is kept in\n  [case-studies/issue-11/plan](case-studies/issue-11/plan/README.md), one file\n  per issue, with the names that the issues share (files, functions, formats).\n- `node experiments/issue-11-create-issues.mjs check` validates the plan: every\n  issue has all sections, every blocker exists and the dependencies have no\n  cycle. `create` made the GitHub issues, milestones and \"blocked by\" links;\n  `update` sends an issue again after its plan file was edited; `roadmap`\n  writes the tables and the graph above from\n  [the list of created issues](case-studies/issue-11/data/created-issues.json).\n- A pull request that finishes an issue ticks nothing here: the state of an\n  issue lives on GitHub. A pull request that changes the direction updates\n  [VISION.md](VISION.md) and adds or edits issues, then this file.\nThe draft implementation of [#62](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/62)\nexports `findLandmarks`, `createLandmarkDetector` and `BROAD_CLASSES`, with\nmel sonority, two-scale band landmarks and a calibrated fixed class tree.\nIt remains unfinished: even the unrestricted voiced maxima cover only\n98/120 synthetic reference nuclei (81.67%), below the 90% gate, and deciding\nwhether a silence run is a closure conflicts with immutable classes at\n60 ms. The [investigation](case-studies/issue-62/README.md) contains executable\ncounterexamples; the acceptance targets remain unchanged.\n\nThe batch source analysis of [#61](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/61)\n(`inverseFilter`) removes an all-pole tract with four-stage IAIF, then measures\nLF Rd, open and normalized amplitude quotients, speech/source H1-H2, HNR and CPP.\nIt accepts the pitch track of #59 or uses local autocorrelation, reports closure\ninstants and reliable-frame quartiles, and flags recordings missing the low band.\nSteady phonation gets an LF-constrained tract refinement. The same numerical code\nis in the Rust core with WebAssembly parity tests. Definitions, measured limits\n/** Public-API counterexample to simultaneous 60 ms immutable commitment\n * and retrospective closure cleanup. Finite input: two one-second signals.\n * Run: node --max-old-space-size=64 experiments/issue-62/stream-closure.mjs\n * Passing assertions prove the incompatibility, not detector acceptance. */\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport {\n  analyzeFrames,\n  createFrameAnalyzer,\n  createLandmarkDetector,\n  findLandmarks,\n} from '../../src/index.js';\n\nconst rate = 8000;\nconst hop = 0.005;\nconst frameTime = 0.36;\nconst commitmentDeadline = frameTime + 0.06;\n// Supply the front end's 12.5 ms window lookahead, too. The two signals\n// still agree through this later point, before either return to speech.\nconst suppliedThrough = commitmentDeadline + 0.0125;\nconst prefixSamples = Math.round(suppliedThrough * rate);\nconst target = Math.round(frameTime / hop);\nconst speechReturns = [0.44, 0.6];\nconst signals = speechReturns.map((resume) => {\n  const samples = new Float32Array(rate);\n  for (let n = 0; n < samples.length; n++) {\n    const time = n / rate;\n    if (\n      (time >= 0.1 && time < 0.3) ||\n      (time >= resume && time < resume + 0.2)\n    ) {\n      samples[n] = 0.1 * Math.sin((2 * Math.PI * 140 * n) / rate);\n    }\n  }\n  return samples;\n});\nassert.deepEqual(\n  signals[0].subarray(0, prefixSamples),\n  signals[1].subarray(0, prefixSamples)\n);\nconst required = signals.map((samples) =>\n  findLandmarks(analyzeFrames(samples, rate)).classes.at(target)\n);\nassert.deepEqual(required, [6, 0]);\nconst streams = signals.map((samples) => {\n  const analyzer = createFrameAnalyzer(rate, { maxSeconds: 1 });\n  const detector = createLandmarkDetector(analyzer.frames);\n  analyzer.push(samples.subarray(0, prefixSamples));\n  detector.advance();\n  assert(detector.output.committed > target);\n  return { analyzer, detector, samples };\n});\nfor (const [key, width] of [\n  ['energy', 1],\n  ['noise', 1],\n  ['periodicity', 1],\n  ['speech', 1],\n  ['zcr', 1],\n  ['gravity', 1],\n  ['tilt', 1],\n  ['band', 6],\n  ['mel', streams[0].analyzer.frames.melBands],\n]) {\n  const a = streams[0].analyzer.frames;\n  const b = streams[1].analyzer.frames;\n  assert.equal(a.count, b.count);\n  assert.deepEqual(\n    a[key].subarray(0, a.count * width),\n    b[key].subarray(0, b.count * width)\n  );\n}\nconst atDeadline = streams.map((s) => s.detector.output.classes.at(target));\nassert.equal(atDeadline[0], atDeadline[1]);\nfor (const { analyzer, detector, samples } of streams) {\n  analyzer.push(samples.subarray(prefixSamples));\n  analyzer.flush();\n  detector.advance(true);\n}\nconst final = streams.map((s) => s.detector.output.classes.at(target));\nassert.deepEqual(final, atDeadline);\nassert.notDeepEqual(final, required);\nconsole.log(\n  JSON.stringify({\n    frameTime,\n    commitmentDeadline,\n    suppliedThrough,\n    speechReturns,\n    requiredBatchClasses: required,\n    committedStreamClasses: atDeadline,\n    finalStreamClasses: final,\n  })\n);\nimport { describe, it, expect } from 'test-anywhere';\nimport {\n  createLandmarkDetector,\n  findLandmarks,\n} from '../src/recognition/landmarks.js';\nimport { boundaryFrames } from './helpers/landmark-frames.js';\n\nfunction checkStrengths(result) {\n  expect(result.nuclei.length).toBe(2);\n  for (const nucleus of result.nuclei) {\n    if (nucleus.end === null) {\n      continue;\n    }\n    const at = (time) => Math.round((time - result.startTime) / result.hop);\n    const expected =\n      result.sonority[at(nucleus.time)] -\n      Math.min(\n        result.sonority[at(nucleus.start)],\n        result.sonority[at(nucleus.end)]\n      );\n    expect(nucleus.strength).toBe(expected);\n  }\n}\n\ndescribe('landmark nucleus boundaries', () => {\n  it('updates strength when the next peak reveals a deeper minimum', () => {\n    const result = findLandmarks(boundaryFrames());\n    expect(result.nuclei[0].end).not.toBe(null);\n    checkStrengths(result);\n  });\n  it('keeps strengths consistent with trailing nonspeech', () => {\n    checkStrengths(findLandmarks(boundaryFrames(true)));\n  });\n  it('keeps streamed strengths consistent with completed boundaries', () => {\n    const frames = boundaryFrames(true);\n    const count = frames.count;\n    frames.count = 0;\n    const detector = createLandmarkDetector(frames);\n    for (let end = 4; end < count; end += 4) {\n      frames.count = end;\n      detector.advance();\n    }\n    frames.count = count;\n    detector.advance(true);\n    checkStrengths(detector.output);\n  });\n});\n .changeset/issue-62-landmarks.md              |   5 +\n .github/workflows/release.yml                 |   2 +-\n README.md                                     |   6 +-\n bin/voice-simulator.js                        |  25 +\n crates/voice-simulator-core/src/landmarks.rs  | 535 +++++++++++++++++++\n crates/voice-simulator-core/src/lib.rs        |   2 +\n crates/voice-simulator-wasm/src/landmarks.rs  |  78 +++\n crates/voice-simulator-wasm/src/lib.rs        |   1 +\n docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md                 |  51 ++\n docs/ROADMAP.md                               |   9 +\n docs/RUST-ENGINE.md                           |  32 +-\n docs/case-studies/README.md                   |  13 +-\n docs/case-studies/issue-62/README.md          | 716 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n docs/case-studies/issue-62/golden-report.json | 173 +++++++\n docs/case-studies/issue-62/golden-report.md   |  35 ++\n docs/reports/recognition-pitch.json           |   3 +-\n experiments/issue-62/accuracy-ceiling.mjs     |  85 +++\n experiments/issue-62/causality.mjs            |  26 +\n experiments/issue-62/class-search.mjs         | 115 +++++\n experiments/issue-62/confirmation.mjs         |  70 +++\n experiments/issue-62/edge-feasibility.mjs     | 100 ++++\n experiments/issue-62/edge-signals.mjs         |  31 ++\n experiments/issue-62/landmark-candidates.mjs  |  63 +++\n experiments/issue-62/nucleus-ceiling.mjs      | 124 +++++\n experiments/issue-62/plan.md                  | 144 ++++++\n experiments/issue-62/probe.mjs                |  42 ++\n experiments/issue-62/stream-candidates.mjs    |  28 +\n experiments/issue-62/stream-closure.mjs       |  91 ++++\n experiments/issue-62/stream-landmarks.mjs     |  56 ++\n scripts/build-wasm.mjs                        |  24 +-\n scripts/calibrate-landmarks.mjs               | 167 ++++++\n scripts/fetch-anatomy.mjs                     |  40 +-\n scripts/fetch-dvtd.mjs                        |  71 ++-\n scripts/landmark-material.mjs                 | 170 ++++++\n src/index.d.ts                                |  13 +\n src/index.js                                  |   7 +\n src/recognition/landmark-nuclei.js            | 145 ++++++\n src/recognition/landmark-signals.js           | 303 +++++++++++\n src/recognition/landmark-thresholds.js        |  20 +\n src/recognition/landmarks.d.ts                |  62 +++\n src/recognition/landmarks.js                  | 174 +++++++\n tests/archive-download.test.js                | 166 ++++++\n tests/cli-audio.test.js                       |  18 +\n tests/dental.test.js                          |  39 +-\n tests/engine-size.test.js                     |   4 +-\n tests/geometry-analysis.test.js               |  20 +-\n tests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js     |  70 +++\n tests/helpers/landmark-frames.js              |  69 +++\n tests/helpers/remote-anatomy.js               |  44 ++\n tests/recognition-landmark-boundaries.test.js |  47 ++\n tests/recognition-landmark-streaming.test.js  |  42 ++\n tests/recognition-landmarks.test.js           | 324 ++++++++++++\n tests/rust-landmarks.test.js                  | 146 ++++++\n 53 files changed, 4763 insertions(+), 83 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
