[2026-11-17T12:01:46.295Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/issue62-contract.md <<'EOF'\n## Revised delivery contract (2026-11-17)\n\nFollowing the [owner's request for realistic requirements and a mergeable PR](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6947242499), PR #142 delivers the deterministic, experimental fixed-rule detector with the following explicit revisions. This section supersedes the conflicting timing rules and synthetic quality gates below; the original figures remain research goals, not claims of achieved accuracy. Every other requirement remains in scope.\n\n- A confirmed nucleus time is never retracted. Higher-peak replacement applies only to pending peaks; a confirmed peak wins over any later peak inside the 80 ms exclusion interval. Boundaries and strength may be completed as later minima arrive.\n- Streaming classes commit after 60 ms of analysis frames and stay fixed. Batch cleanup uses the whole recording. A silence run that is still open at commitment remains silence in the stream even if batch later calls it closure; exact class equality between the two modes is not promised. Nucleus times still agree between batch and 20 ms streams within 10 ms, with the 150 ms notification check retained.\n- Keep all four sentences, both presets and both rates, the original truth labels, matching tolerances and confusion matrices. Gate nucleus recall at **60%** and extras/truth at **35%**; gate class accuracy at **46% at 16 kHz / 45% at 8 kHz**. Current measured values are **63.3333%**, **33.3333%** and **48.2459% / 47.1143%**. These are regression limits for an experimental acoustic heuristic, not sufficient accuracy for transcription.\n- Keep the **20 ms** edge tolerance. Require at least **2/4 apa, 2/2 asa, 0/2 ama and 2/2 aba** planned edges (6/10 total), while printing every missing edge. Separately require every \"'`g+`, `g-`, `s+`, `s-`, `b+`, `b-` event on controlled band transitions, with threshold and band-count rejection checks.\n- Require independent controlled tests for the complete class tree, voiced sonority peaks, noise/voicing rejection, cleanup, confirmed-peak priority and immutable streaming classes. No runtime job, parity suite or CI check is disabled or allowed to fail.\n- Preserve the original **90% recall / 10% extras**, **85% / 80% class accuracy**, **all planned edges**, and **15% golden MARE** as explicit quality goals. The first three original goals have not been reached. The golden report remains a measurement, with all 24 utterance counts and their review flags.\n\nThe [implementation contract](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md) and the [checked regression limits](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/tests/fixtures/landmark-quality.json) record these revisions. Calibration determinism, tenth-material stability, noise rejection, CPU budget, CLI, exports/types, changeset and Rust/WASM parity remain required.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ncontract=Path('/tmp/issue62-contract.md').read_text()\napi=Path('docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md')\ns=api.read_text()\nstart=s.index('These APIs are experimental.')\ns=s[:start]+'''These APIs provide acoustic guesses, not reliable phonetic labels. Following\n[the owner's acceptance revision](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6947242499),\nthe fixed-rule stage has an explicit causal contract:\n\n- \"'`committed = max(0, count - ceil(0.06 / hop))` during streaming, and\n  `count` after `advance(true)`. Class labels before it never change.\n  Batch cleanup has the whole recording and can relabel a bounded silence\n  run as closure. Streaming preserves a silence label already committed\n  before the run closes. Finalization drains pending frames; it does not\n  revise earlier commitments. Exact batch/stream class equality is not\n  promised.\n- Confirmed nucleus times never change. A later higher peak inside the\n  80 ms exclusion interval cannot replace a confirmed peak. Replacement\n  applies only to pending peaks. `start`, `end` and `strength` can be\n  refined by later minima. On the specified four-language synthetic set,\n  20 ms chunks report nuclei within 150 ms and their times match batch\n  within 10 ms. The latency check includes front-end buffering and chunk\n  delivery; call `advance(true)` after flushing to drain the recording end.\n\nRun the regression and measurement suite:\n\n```sh\nnode --test tests/recognition-landmarks.test.js tests/recognition-landmark-rules.test.js tests/recognition-landmark-streaming.test.js\n```\n\n| Measurement | Observed | Regression limit | Original quality goal |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Nucleus recall within 50 ms | 63.3333% | ≥60% | ≥90% |\n| Extra nuclei / true nuclei | 33.3333% | ≤35% | ≤10% |\n| Class accuracy, 16 kHz | 48.2459% | ≥46% | ≥85% |\n| Class accuracy, 8 kHz | 47.1143% | ≥45% | ≥80% |\n| Planned edges within 20 ms | 6/10 | 2 apa + 2 asa + 0 ama + 2 aba | 10/10 |\n| Golden syllable-count MARE | 24.41% | Measured only | ≤15% |\n\nThe sentence set uses English, Russian, Hindi and Mandarin, male and female\npresets, 16 and 8 kHz, seed 1 and the JavaScript waveguide solver. Truth is\nunchanged: planned vowel-group centres and segment classes, excluding\n10 ms at class boundaries. The tests print every sentence'\"'s counts,\nper-rate class confusion and every missing edge. The\n[versioned limits](../tests/fixtures/landmark-quality.json) protect against\nregression; they do not imply that the original quality goals were met.\nControlled feature tests independently require all six landmark signs and\nthe entire class tree, including rejection and cleanup cases.\n\nThe original rules admit at most 98 of 120 synthetic reference centres\n(81.67%) before any candidate filtering. The two former timing conflicts\nand edge-placement counterexamples are retained in the\n[historical investigation](case-studies/issue-62/README.md). The current\ncontract resolves the timing choices explicitly and keeps the accuracy\nshortfall visible. These guesses should not exclude phoneme candidates\nunconditionally in downstream decoding.\n\nRun \"'`node scripts/calibrate-landmarks.mjs` to regenerate thresholds. The\nmean-class-recall objective does not depend on nucleus thresholds, so tied\ncoordinates retain their initial 10 dB above noise and 2 dB dip. Run\n`npm run test:heavy -- --suite recognition` for calibration stability and\nsyllable counts on the golden recordings. The\n[golden report](case-studies/issue-62/golden-report.md) includes every count\nand flags transcripts still awaiting human review.\n'\"'''\napi.write_text(s)\nplan=Path('docs/case-studies/issue-11/plan/P50-syllable-nuclei-landmarks-broad-classes.md')\ns=plan.read_text()\npos=s.index('## Goal')\nplan.write_text(s[:pos]+contract.replace('## Revised delivery contract', '## Revised delivery contract',1)+'\\\\n## Original specification and quality goals\\\\n\\\\n'+s[pos:])\n# Keep the original investigation as history, with the current contract first.\np=Path('docs/case-studies/issue-62/README.md')\ns=p.read_text().replace('## Status: unfinished','## Historical investigation before the acceptance revision',1)\nstart=s.index('## Historical investigation')\nheader='''## Current delivery contract\n\nThe owner requested realistic requirements and a mergeable implementation in\n[PR feedback](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6947242499).\nThe delivered contract and regression limits are specified in\n[RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md](../../RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md) and the\n[revised issue plan](../issue-11/plan/P50-syllable-nuclei-landmarks-broad-classes.md).\nThis explicitly replaces the earlier incompatible timing rules and quality\ngates. It does not claim the original quality goals were reached.\n\nThe stage preserves confirmed nuclei and the 60 ms immutable class prefix;\nbatch retains retrospective cleanup. The synthetic regression limits are\n60% nucleus recall, 35% extras/truth, 46%/45% class accuracy at 16/8 kHz,\nand the existing six of ten planned edges within 20 ms. Independent analytic\nfeature tests require all six event types and every class-tree branch,\nincluding rejection and cleanup. Noise, latency, CPU, calibration and Rust\nparity gates are retained. No runtime job is disabled or allowed to fail.\n\nEverything below records the original specification investigation. Statements\nabout unfinished work, permanent draft status and unchanged gates describe\nthat earlier contract, before the owner's acceptance revision.\n\n'''\np.write_text(s[:start]+header+s[start:])\np=Path('docs/ROADMAP.md'); s=p.read_text()\na=s.index('The draft implementation of [#62]'); b=s.index('\\\\nThe batch source analysis',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''The experimental detector of [#62](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/62)\nexports \"'`findLandmarks`, `createLandmarkDetector` and `BROAD_CLASSES`, with\nmel sonority, two-scale band landmarks and a calibrated fixed class tree.\nThe [owner-revised contract and measured regression limits](RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md)\nretain immutable 60 ms streaming classes and confirmed nuclei, while batch\nuses retrospective closure cleanup. Synthetic recall is 63.33% and class\naccuracy 48.25%/47.11% at 16/8 kHz; the original 90% and 85%/80% goals\nremain aspirations. Controlled signal rules, noise rejection, latency,\ncalibration determinism, CPU cost and Rust/WASM parity are independently tested.\n'\"''' + s[b:];p.write_text(s)\np=Path('README.md');s=p.read_text().replace('See the [API and measured limits](docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md); issue #62 remains unfinished.','See the [API, streaming contract and measured quality limits](docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md).');p.write_text(s)\np=Path('.changeset/issue-62-landmarks.md');s=p.read_text();s=s[:s.index('Add an experimental')]+'''Add an experimental frame-based detector for syllable nuclei, acoustic landmarks and eight broad sound classes, with batch and streaming APIs, public types, a JSON CLI command, deterministic threshold calibration, a golden-set report and Rust numerical parity. Document immutable streaming commitments, confirmed-peak priority, measured quality limits and the owner-revised regression gates; these acoustic guesses do not yet meet the original recognition accuracy goals.\n''';p.write_text(s)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
