[2026-11-17T12:07:59.277Z] [STDERR] [{"body":"Identify English, Russian, Hindi and Mandarin directly from IPA and locate language changes inside an utterance. Pass the identified spans into `ipaToText` to decode all involved lexicons together and retain a language on each word.\n\nFixes #69\n\nThe model derives count-weighted phone unigrams, bigrams and trigrams lazily from existing pronunciation tries. Syllable scoring, tone cues, pause-aware Viterbi, island smoothing and ambiguous-span lexical comparison determine spans, confidence and speech shares. `languageShares(words)` recomputes shares after transcription. Library exports, TypeScript types and `voice-simulator language` expose the feature; a minor changeset prepares the release.\n\nMixed decoding charges span mismatch/switch costs, resets bigram context after language changes and joins adjacent Mandarin words without spaces. Final calibration remains 0.6/0.3/0.1 interpolation, 0.0001 floor, tone cue 3, switch penalty 6 (half at pauses), lexical gap 0.5/sound, span mismatch 1 and word-language switch 1. A bounded calibration experiment (`node experiments/issue-69-word-boundaries.mjs`) reduced the starting mismatch cost from 2 to 1, improving exact word recovery from 63/75 (84%) to 64/75 (85.33%) without changing any requested threshold or recognition data. The new exact-word regression test fails before this adjustment and passes afterward.\n\nRust mirrors the numerical model and joint search. WASM parity compares small deterministic lexicons, paths, local costs, scores, confidence and duration shares within 1e-10 and rejects malformed packets. Current `main` is merged; its acoustics features are preserved. Combined engine sizes are 435,525 scalar and 442,832 SIMD bytes (Rust 1.100.0), with the measured budget rounded to 458,752 bytes.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```sh\nnode bin/voice-simulator.js language 'ɐˈna skɐˈzaɫə ˈθæŋk ˈju i ˈuʂɫə'\n# ru 0-10 1.00\n# en 10-16 0.75\n# ru 16-
