[2026-11-17T12:07:59.297Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_107","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat ci-logs/pr-style.json && node -e 'const p=JSON.parse(require(\\\"fs\\\").readFileSync(\\\"ci-logs/pr142-latest.json\\\")); console.log(p.title, p.isDraft, p.headRefOid); console.log(p.comments.slice(-3).map(c=>({url:c.url,body:c.body})));' && sed -n '1,210p' src/recognition/landmarks.js && cat src/recognition/landmarks.d.ts\"","aggregated_output":"[{\"body\":\"Identify English, Russian, Hindi and Mandarin directly from IPA and locate language changes inside an utterance. Pass the identified spans into `ipaToText` to decode all involved lexicons together and retain a language on each word.\\n\\nFixes #69\\n\\nThe model derives count-weighted phone unigrams, bigrams and trigrams lazily from existing pronunciation tries. Syllable scoring, tone cues, pause-aware Viterbi, island smoothing and ambiguous-span lexical comparison determine spans, confidence and speech shares. `languageShares(words)` recomputes shares after transcription. Library exports, TypeScript types and `voice-simulator language` expose the feature; a minor changeset prepares the release.\\n\\nMixed decoding charges span mismatch/switch costs, resets bigram context after language changes and joins adjacent Mandarin words without spaces. Final calibration remains 0.6/0.3/0.1 interpolation, 0.0001 floor, tone cue 3, switch penalty 6 (half at pauses), lexical gap 0.5/sound, span mismatch 1 and word-language switch 1. A bounded calibration experiment (`node experiments/issue-69-word-boundaries.mjs`) reduced the starting mismatch cost from 2 to 1, improving exact word recovery from 63/75 (84%) to 64/75 (85.33%) without changing any requested threshold or recognition data. The new exact-word regression test fails before this adjustment and passes afterward.\\n\\nRust mirrors the numerical model and joint search. WASM parity compares small deterministic lexicons, paths, local costs, scores, confidence and duration shares within 1e-10 and rejects malformed packets. Current `main` is merged; its acoustics features are preserved. Combined engine sizes are 435,525 scalar and 442,832 SIMD bytes (Rust 1.100.0), with the measured budget rounded to 458,752 bytes.\\n\\n### Reproduce\\n\\n```sh\\nnode bin/voice-simulator.js language 'ɐˈna skɐˈzaɫə ˈθæŋk ˈju i ˈuʂɫə'\\n# ru 0-10 1.00\\n# en 10-16 0.75\\n# ru 16-21 0.60\\nnode --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/language-id.test.js\\nnode experiments/issue-69-measure.mjs\\n```\\n\\nThe twelve fixtures (three per en+ru, en+hi, en+zh and ru+zh pair) are [posted on the issue](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/69#issuecomment-6944915200) and committed in `tests/fixtures/recognition/mixed-sentences.json`. Expected languages come from `textToIpa(...).words[].lang`. Latin words read as pinyin by the forward converter are not treated as English. Mandarin decoded units use phonological syllables, following #68, to allow equivalent character segmentation; other units are words. Sound and language errors, insertions and deletions all count. A separate exact-word gate counts segmentation errors in all four languages and enforces the requested 85% without syllable alignment.\\n\\n### Measurements\\n\\nNode.js 26.13.0, 2026-11-17; tests print every measurement and enforce each threshold.\\n\\n| Check | Measured | Required |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Monolingual sentences | 40/40 (100%) | 100% |\\n| English words with at least four sounds | 1997/2000 (99.85%) | 90% |\\n| Russian words | 2000/2000 (100%) | 90% |\\n| Hindi words | 2000/2000 (100%) | 90% |\\n| Mandarin words with tones | 2000/2000 (100%) | 97% |\\n| Mandarin sentences without tones | 10/10 (100%) | 90% |\\n| Mixed word languages | 69/75 (92.00%) | 90% |\\n| Exact decoded words, sounds and language | 64/75 (85.33%) | 85% |\\n| Joint decoded sounds/languages, syllable alignment | 76/79 (96.20%) | 85% |\\n| Mixed span counts | Every fixture ≤ true count + 1 | ≤ true count + 1 |\\n| English continuity | 30 syllables, 1 span | 1 span |\\n| Three-sound confidence | 0.1503647386 | Below 0.5 |\\n| Seed-1 nearest-sound substitutions, 10% chance/sound | 67/75 (89.33%) | ≥75%; regression gate 87.33% |\\n| Warm 120 sounds, no lexical comparisons | 2.209 ms | <50 ms |\\n| CLI acceptance | ru → en → ru | ru → en → ru |\\n\\nWord confusion matrix (rows true, columns predicted):\\n\\n| | en | ru | hi | zh |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n| en | 1997 | 1 | 1 | 1 |\\n| ru | 0 | 2000 | 0 | 0 |\\n| hi | 0 | 0 | 2000 | 0 |\\n| zh | 0 | 0 | 0 | 2000 |\\n\\n### Validation\\n\\n- 61 focused tests passed: acceptance, monolingual compatibility, CLI audio, engine size and JS/WASM parity. Timed input, pause exclusion, option validation and model arithmetic are covered.\\n- Full local sequential run: 3,048 passed, 15 skipped, one existing WASM-enabled CLI error-message failure. Aligned the Rust error wording with the existing CLI contract; that regression passes in the focused run.\\n- `npm run check` passed. [Final CI run 44065057347](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44065057347) is green at `d94f5f5`: all nine Node.js/Bun/Deno × Linux/macOS/Windows combinations passed, together with Rust, lint, documentation, compilation, simulation, file-size and release checks. The final-commit example-app, security and link workflows also passed.\\n- Sequential local Rust build and clippy passed; no dependencies or recognition count data added.\\n- [Unlimited Heavy performance run 44061935584](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44061935584): 75/75 tests passed, no skips. Its artifact updates the performance trend and engine-parity report; the baseline is unchanged. This run measured `3badd0f`; subsequent code changes only tune transcription costs and align invalid-source diagnostics, leaving audio rendering unchanged.\\n- `git diff --stat origin/main -- src/recognition/data` is empty; the requested dependency-name scan prints nothing.\\n\\n[API, calibration and measurement details](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-69-747cdfb224e7/docs/language-id.md).\\n\",\"number\":147,\"title\":\"Identify IPA languages and decode mixed speech\"},{\"body\":\"Closes #82\\n\\nThe Rust engine now renders vocal folds, source-tract and subglottal coupling, whisper and the 2D sheet without handing feature requests to JavaScript. Its executable inventory also covers noise, losses, phonation, effort, articulators, listeners and narrowband tiers.\\n\\n- Add 18 frozen feature entries, compiled Rust/WASM/native capability reporting, and a build-free bidirectional inventory check in `npm run check` and Rust CI. Every acoustics module is registered or has a documented `JS_ONLY` reason.\\n- Port the missing physics in separate commits and extend the renderer ABI to version 5. Every feature retains the maximum sample error of `1e-4`; no spectrum exemption or relaxed tolerance is needed. The JavaScript reference sound is unchanged.\\n- Remove missing-feature handoffs and expose `fallbacks` plus load-failure reasons. Custom solvers and browser WebGPU remain available through an explicit JavaScript engine. Planning, static anatomy construction and offline analysis remain in the host.\\n- Preserve fold-source transferable state, chunked 2D fields and 3D glottal-load reset. Correct model-header offsets so direct WASM packing returns the complete pressure field. Keep the source-analysis, formant and IPA-recognition APIs merged from main.\\n- Enforce scalar, single-thread speed for all 18 features and all 10 tiers, including `reference`. Pack large 3D opening tables directly into WASM memory with identical bytes. The scalar FDTD loop advances through private, validated arrays; its narrowly scoped unsafe block has documented invariants, constructor rejection tests and an architecture check. Native and SIMD loops keep their existing implementation.\\n- Add generated native reference vectors, combined folds/whisper/nasal/interaction cases across all three CPU solvers, documentation, types, CLI help and a minor changeset.\\n\\nTo reproduce the original missing paths, request `createEngine('rust')` and render `source: 'folds'`, `interaction: true`, whisper IPA or `solver: 'fdtd2d'`. Previously these requests used JavaScript. `tests/engine-parity.test.js` now has 33 numerical/API checks, including every feature, Rust renderer identity and zero fallbacks. Native tests compare five ported features with JS-generated vectors. The fold-source state, native reset and direct-packed field regressions fail before their fixes and pass afterward. The field test compares nonzero, finite pressures after 2,400 samples; packing tests cover reused aligned and unaligned buffers.\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- [Complete implementation CI](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44057942673) on `a55c663`: all nine Node/Bun/Deno × Linux/macOS/Windows jobs pass, plus Rust workspace tests, clippy, formatting, WASM builds and parity checks. The Bun/macOS architecture test now compares its allow list independently of filesystem order; the existing anatomy download test also passes.\\n- [Final documentation CI](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44059499938) on `3f874f3` passes. This commit changes measured reports, the case-study record and removal of the generated PR placeholder only.\\n- [Complete performance suite](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44055371834), commit `908f7f7`: all five files and 75 tests pass with no item limit. All 28 Rust/JS medians are <= 1.0 (range 0.4675–0.9237); coarse 3D is 0.8803 and the reference tier is 0.9237. Raw data was checked for complete, unique coverage, finite timings, at least two seconds per engine, at least three runs, and independently recomputed medians and ratios. The scalar build SHA-256 `ef1addd5307bace6722a10802d027671888305dec3db8ea8918f3be615edd653` matches the rebuilt implementation after the subsequent test and safety-comment changes.\\n- Local focused checks pass: 50 WASM parity/FDTD/size/architecture checks, two native constructor/reset regressions, 29 post-merge feature/size/IPA-recognition checks, the strengthened nonzero field regression, and all 13 performance tracking tests after generating the updated history. Report formatting and file line limits pass.\\n\\nThe [committed performance report](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-82-b17ba5b63341/docs/reports/engine-parity.md) contains the measured table and run/commit provenance. The same passing artifact appends the [performance history](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-82-b17ba5b63341/docs/reports/performance.md), preserving all six runs. Failed speed runs, their root causes, the field/reset regressions and bounded experiments are recorded in [the case study](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-82-b17ba5b63341/docs/case-studies/issue-82/plan.md).\\n\\nMain `0b6c090` is merged. The working tree is clean. All final-head status checks pass; the PR is ready for review and remains unmerged.\\n\",\"number\":145,\"title\":\"Complete Rust engine parity and enforce feature coverage\"},{\"body\":\"Decode IPA into English, Russian, Hindi and Mandarin text through cached pronunciation tries, bounded edit search and public-domain word/bigram counts. The typed `ipaToText` API accepts strings or timed sounds, restores boundaries, returns word/syllable timing and confidence, and supports distinct alternative texts. `voice-simulator text <ipa> --lang <code>` exposes the same decoder.\\n\\nFixes #68\\n\\n- Builds count tables offline from 1,473,964 / 1,145,974 / 1,103,787 / 1,683,196 accepted source words (en/ru/hi/zh). Every source, author, publication year, public-domain basis and exact processed SHA-256 is recorded in [SOURCES.md](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-68-60e84c80a49f/src/recognition/data/SOURCES.md). Raw texts stay outside Git and are never downloaded in CI.\\n- Each language contains 20,000 descending word counts and 40,000 observed bigrams with count at least three. Files are 591267 / 751674 / 773343 / 618231 bytes, all below 800000. `du -k src/recognition/data` reports 2700 KiB, below 3200. The required dependency-name scan prints nothing; ordinary corpus words use lossless escapes where necessary.\\n- Derives pronunciations from the current forward rules and every lexicon variant, including Hindi schwas and Russian clitics. Explicit spelling rules handle unknown words in all four scripts; Mandarin inverts every listed reading. Shared orthography helpers give the same syllable spelling as the timeline.\\n- Implements the numerical distance, trie/edit search, discounted count scoring and beam decoding in the Rust core with additive WebAssembly exports. Six parity checks compare all 12100 phone pairs, four languages, edits, boundary modes, unknown words, distinct alternatives and malformed packets. Absolute tolerances are 1e-12 for distances and 1e-10 for decoding costs.\\n- Adds API/types, CLI/help, README/roadmap, [algorithm and measured results](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-68-60e84c80a49f/docs/ipa-to-text.md), and a minor changeset. Latest main is merged with its source-analysis, formant and codebook APIs and tests preserved.\\n\\n### Final costs\\n\\nVowels: height 2, backness 1.5, rounding 0.5, length/nasality 0.3. Consonants: manner 0.5, place 0.35 per normalized distance in the twelve-place list, voicing 0.25, aspiration/palatalisation 0.2. Coarticulated places use the nearer place. Cross-kind distance is 1 (i/j and u/w: 0.6). Tone adds 0.5, except third/half-third 0 and third/rising 0.15; stress adds 0.2. Total distance is capped at 1. Insert/delete costs are 1, or 0.5 for schwa/glottal stop.\\n\\nCandidate cutoff: `0.6 * (sounds used + 1)`. Approximate acoustic weight: 10. Unknown cost: `3 + 2 * sounds`, at most twelve sounds; an exactly readable suffix can propose a shorter unknown boundary. Word cost: `-0.3 * ln(P) + 0.5`, discount 0.75, unigram backoff 0.4. A complete exact path takes precedence. These documented calibrations prevent noisy phrases from collapsing into unrelated long words.\\n\\n### Reproduction and automated verification\\n\\nThe [forty fixed sentences posted in the issue](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/68#issuecomment-6941363838) are committed fixtures, each with 5–10 words. They are evaluation inputs and are not added to the corpus. Local Node.js 26.13.0 results from:\\n\\n```sh\\nnode --test --test-timeout=30000 --test-concurrency=1 \\\\\\n  tests/ipa-to-text.test.js tests/recognition-data.test.js \\\\\\n  tests/rust-recognition.test.js tests/engine-size.test.js tests/lexicon.test.js\\n```\\n\\nAll 50 checks pass. `node experiments/issue-68/measure.mjs` reproduces the accuracy measurements.\\n\\n| Language | First 5000, same sounds | Same spelling | Sentence spelling | Unspaced boundaries by sound | Seed-1 noisy WER | 200 held-out words, same sounds | Cold trie |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| en | 5000/5000 | 4874/5000 (97.48%) | 69/69 (100%) | 69/69 (100%) | 0/69 (0%) | 166/200 (83%) | 1.524 s |\\n| ru | 5000/5000 | 4835/5000 (96.70%) | 52/53 (98.11%) | 52/53 (98.11%) | 3/53 (5.66%) | 191/200 (95.5%) | 1.918 s |\\n| hi | 5000/5000 | 4873/5000 (97.46%) | 65/66 (98.48%) | 65/66 (98.48%) | 6/66 (9.09%) | 200/200 (100%) | 1.222 s |\\n| zh | 5000/5000 | 4896/5000 (97.92%) | 106/112 (94.64%) | 110/112 (98.21%) | 22/112 (19.64%) | 191/200 (95.5%) | 1.812 s |\\n\\nAll forty sentences retain the same sounds. Mandarin boundary/noise comparisons use the forward engine's character syllables; spelling uses characters. Thus compound-word grouping does not count as a phonetic error. Every noise regression gate is the measured fraction plus 0.02, with a strict 30% cap. Held-out tests remove all entries for the 200 words from the reverse trie before invoking the rule speller. Homophones and polyphonic character defaults explain remaining ambiguity; arbitrary isolated spelling recovery is not asserted.\\n\\nThe warmed 120-sound query at beam 8 takes 3.2 ms (limit 500 ms). Every cold trie is below three seconds. Profiling found array allocations in the compressed lexicon's Unicode comparator: a bounded 200000-comparison experiment fell from 79.59 to 8.91 ms with identical ordering checksum; supplementary characters and prefixes have regression coverage. All inventory pairs pass symmetry/bounds/identity checks. `two cats` wins its homophone case, unknown `blik` has confidence at most 0.3, `hello` splits into `hel` / `lo`, and timed sounds retain times and confidence. Scalar/SIMD WebAssembly sizes are 332646 / 338849 bytes within the 336 KiB budget.\\n\\n```sh\\nnode bin/voice-simulator.js text 'həˈloʊ ˈwɝld' --lang en # hello world\\nnode bin/voice-simulator.js text 'prʲɪˈvʲet' --lang ru    # привет\\nnode bin/voice-simulator.js text 'ni˧˥ xɑʊ˨˩˦' --lang zh # 你好\\n```\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- Local `npm run check`, focused Rust recognition tests, workspace clippy, rustfmt, scalar/SIMD builds and WebAssembly parity pass. After the latest main merge, all 25 combined recognition, formant and engine parity checks pass.\\n- The [full performance suite](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44048569212) passes all 46 checks without an item limit: waveguide/FDTD, native/WebAssembly threading and all nine audio tiers. Its artifact adds the `8bb2a50` row to the committed performance trend; the baseline is unchanged. Core implementation files are identical in the subsequent test-fixture fix.\\n- All nine [Node/Bun/Deno platform jobs](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44050048847) pass on Linux, macOS and Windows, together with Rust, lint/format, documentation, size, changeset, simulation and Docker checks. The sibling [workflow](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44050048750), [security](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44050048743), [example app](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44050048733) and [link](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44050049030) workflows also pass.\\n\\nThe final report commit `f13fa65` changes documentation and performance history only. Its [checks](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44051780259), [workflow validation](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44051780193), [security](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44051780198), [example app](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44051780271) and [links](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44051780197) all pass. Production code is unchanged from the full runtime and performance runs above.\\n\\nThe first merged matrix exposed a test-fixture import error on all three Bun runners: `Expected undefined to be \\\"torch=4\\\"` (preserved full log lines 21119, 26238 and 38569 of run 44048579286). Importing the generated file in an explicit ES-module fixture passes the same eight count-table checks locally on Bun and Node. The production decoder and count tables are unchanged by this portability fix.\\n\",\"number\":144,\"title\":\"Decode IPA into text in English, Russian, Hindi and Mandarin\"},{\"body\":\"Generate a deterministic articulatory codebook from the simulator on first use. The typed API builds tract positions, formants and spectral envelopes, caches versioned binary bytes, reads LPC frames and returns the best candidate positions through an allocation-free k-d lookup. Open velums use short waveguide renders with the specified neutral-source correction.\\n\\nFixes #64\\n\\n- Includes all vowel/consonant seed proposals, independent seeded sampling, clipping, deduplication, the 10% nasal cap, measured non-uniqueness and defensive binary parsing. Lookup visits at most 192 rows (within the 512-row limit), retains 64 keys and reranks by envelope error.\\n- Pure length scaling differs by 3.69% at 14 cm, above the 2% tolerance. Implements the specified fallback: geometry and cache identity use tract length rounded to 0.5 cm; the direct comparison then differs by at most 1.10%. Identity includes every normalized head field because the forward model uses more than the original four.\\n- The six arrays, including four integers per tree node, use 94 bytes/row: 1,880,080 bytes for 20000 rows. No generated table is shipped.\\n- Adds exported TypeScript types, README/API/CLI/roadmap documentation, a minor changeset, and Rust transfer/key primitives with WebAssembly parity. Rust table generation (#77), temporal inversion (#65) and app worker/storage integration (#74) remain their explicitly separate scope.\\n\\nMeasured by `npm run test:heavy -- --suite recognition` in [recognition CI](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44033806209):\\n\\n| Check | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| 20000-row build | 18.70 s (limit 60 s; target 30 s) |\\n| Mean query | 17.21 microseconds (limit 50) |\\n| Independent unseen plans, F1-F3 within 5% in top 16 | 499/500 (99.8%; required 95%) |\\n| Non-unique rows | **78.53%** |\\n| Rendered vowels at 16/8 kHz | **23/31 (74.19%) / 21/31 (67.74%)** |\\n\\nThe issue's **90% rendered-vowel target is not met**. The raw observation retains source coloration while oral rows describe tract transfer. A bounded front-end parameter sweep reached at most 24/31; explicit neutral-source calibration improved matches to 28/31 and 29/31. Both diagnostics are reproducible under `experiments/issue-64-*.mjs`; the public observation/query formulas remain those specified in the issue. Full measurements and interpretation are preserved in [the report](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-64-91c8bf7d0423/docs/reports/recognition-codebook.md).\\n\\nValidation:\\n\\n- [Node.js/Bun/Deno on Ubuntu/macOS/Windows](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44033759626): all nine jobs passed, each with 200/200 exhaustive-search agreement and identical 2000-row SHA-256 `d09d50f9bb9d90142d61de67cf07703ffe9cf095b0deb50710254f152f02eda3`. Rust Engine built WebAssembly and passed parity.\\n- Local `npm run check`; `node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-timeout=30000 tests/*.test.js` (2818 passed, 82 skipped, no failures); focused Rust tests, workspace clippy and rustfmt. Full Rust workspace tests passed in CI.\\n- `npm pack --dry-run --json`: 202 entries; no generated table or reports. The 20000-row hash agrees between local and CI builds.\\n- [Full performance CI](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44034571807) passed without an item limit: Rust waveguide/FDTD, native/WebAssembly threading and all nine audio tiers. Added its artifact to the performance trend; the baseline is unchanged.\\n- [Final commit checks](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44036441165), [security](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44036441004), [example app](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44036440639) and [links](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44036441105) cover the final documentation commit. The implementation code is unchanged from the full runtime, recognition and performance runs above.\\n\\nCI maintenance: the existing PTDB-TUG reference timed out twice ([logs](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44033759617), timeout at log line 225 and failed retry at line 273). Replaces that report link with the archive identified by the checker; link checking remains enabled.\\n\",\"number\":143,\"title\":\"Generate articulatory codebooks from the simulator\"},{\"body\":\"Fixes #61.\\n\\n`inverseFilter(analyzeFrames(samples, rate), { pitch })` now estimates the vocal-fold flow and derivative from finished speech, locates closures, and returns per-frame Rd, OQ, NAQ, speech/source H1-H2, HNR, CPP, reliability and reliable-frame quartiles. Pitch can come from `trackPitch` or the specified local autocorrelation/median estimator. Missing low-frequency energy disables the source-shape measures while retaining HNR and CPP.\\n\\nThe four-stage IAIF implementation uses the requested LPC orders, zero-phase 50 Hz high-pass, leaky integration and Hann overlap-add. Filter histories are warmed outside the LPC analysis window: resetting them at each block boundary produced artificial impulses and a derivative correlation near 0.14. A documented LF-constrained least-squares tract refinement on stationary voiced runs prevents high-order tract LPC from absorbing the source poles. Changing speech retains IAIF. The refinement uses analytic LF candidates, with no source-truth inputs, closed-phase method, learned model or new dependency.\\n\\nThe same numerical code is implemented in the Rust core and exposed through an additive `vs_inverse_filter` ABI-4 export. JS exports and types, CLI help, README, roadmap, the breathiness audit and a minor changeset are included. [API, algorithm, packed ABI and limitations](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-61-12f3a026e073/docs/INVERSE-FILTER.md) describe the definitions and reproducing commands.\\n\\n### Reproduction and automated verification\\n\\n`tests/recognition-inverse-filter.test.js` generates the issue's seeded 1.5-second LF source through the three specified resonators, retaining the original derivative as truth. It also covers noise, telephone filtering, male/female speech at both rates, local/supplied pitch, absolute times, deterministic results, empty/short/silent inputs, invalid options and unused buffer capacity after trimming. These public exports and tests were absent before this change.\\n\\nRun `node --test tests/recognition-inverse-filter.test.js`, `bun test tests/recognition-inverse-filter.test.js`, or `deno test -A tests/recognition-inverse-filter.test.js`.\\n\\n| Measurement | Required | Local Node result |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Derivative correlation, 16 / 8 kHz | ≥ 0.9 / 0.8 | 0.99594 / 0.99720 |\\n| GCI periods with exactly one closure / within 0.25 ms | ≥ 95% / 80% | 100% / 100% |\\n| HNR with noise 20 dB below five harmonics | 20 ± 3 dB | 19.425 dB |\\n| Clean CPP minus CPP at −5 dB noise | ≥ 4 dB | 7.2124 dB |\\n| Male / female reliable voiced frames, 16 kHz, local pitch | ≥ 60% | 119/174 (68.4%) / 112/173 (64.7%) |\\n| Male / female reliable voiced frames, 16 kHz, supplied pitch | ≥ 60% | 144/145 (99.3%) / 138/145 (95.2%) |\\n\\n### Rd truth and measured accuracy misses\\n\\n#32 changed `lfParameters` to couple Rd to breathiness. For the exact fixture requested here (`breathiness: 0`), the actual source Rd values are now **1.8, 1.2, 0.6**, rather than the issue's earlier **2.1, 1.5, 0.9**. The regression test asserts monotonic ordering and the 0.4 bound against the current generator's actual truth, and prints errors against both sets. This corrects the reference; it does not claim the original nominal targets were achieved.\\n\\n| f0 | Tenseness | Median Rd | Actual truth | Error vs actual | Error vs issue nominal |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| 110 | 0.3 | 1.50 | 1.80 | −0.30 | −0.60 |\\n| 110 | 0.5 | 1.08 | 1.20 | −0.12 | −0.42 |\\n| 110 | 0.7 | 0.54 | 0.60 | −0.06 | −0.36 |\\n| 220 | 0.3 | 1.74 | 1.80 | −0.06 | −0.36 |\\n| 220 | 0.5 | 1.14 | 1.20 | −0.06 | −0.36 |\\n| 220 | 0.7 | 0.54 | 0.60 | −0.06 | −0.36 |\\n\\nAll six meet the 0.4 bound against actual source truth. The 110 Hz / tenseness 0.3 case misses the 0.25 goal; all six miss it against the stale nominal values. These measured misses are reported as the issue explicitly permits. No precision physical-fold fit is claimed.\\n\\n`node experiments/issue-11-audit.mjs` adds a line for each breathiness setting with median inverse-filter HNR/CPP. Both decrease at every step; the new lines are also saved in `experiments/issue-11-audit.txt`:\\n\\n| Breathiness | Median HNR, dB | Median CPP |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 0 | 15.9642 | 3.3428 |\\n| 0.5 | 15.2868 | 1.1606 |\\n| 1 | 7.3600 | 0.8008 |\\n\\n### Runtime, Rust and repository checks\\n\\nThe warmed best-of-three CPU test follows the existing pitch-test protocol and excludes synthesis/front-end work. An isolated Node run with `INVERSE_FILTER_RTF_LIMIT=0.10 node --test --test-name-pattern='stays within the CPU budget' tests/recognition-inverse-filter.test.js` measured **0.0964 RTF**; a later complete focused run measured **0.0869**. The normal test fails above 0.4; a dedicated Ubuntu Node CI step enforces 0.10. `node experiments/issue-61/rtf.mjs` provides a bounded five-run average probe.\\n\\n`tests/rust-inverse-filter.test.js` compares flow, derivative, closures, every measure, summary, NaN mask and reliability mask at both rates, with local/supplied pitch, noisy/custom options, missing low band and empty/silent data. Class B relative RMS is ≤ 1e−6; unreliable fit/source-H1-H2 diagnostics near silence use an explicit absolute 0.002 dB bound because those ratios are ill-conditioned. Reliable diagnostics retain the strict bound. No mask or length tolerance is relaxed.\\n\\nLocal checks pass: focused Node/Bun/Deno tests (11 each); `npm run check`; `taskset -c 0,1 npm test` (2,897 passed, 0 failed, 15 skipped); `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings`; `cargo test --workspace --locked` (92 tests); scalar/SIMD Wasm builds with size checks; and `REQUIRE_WASM=1 node --test tests/rust-inverse-filter.test.js` (5 tests).\\n\\nAfter merging the latest `main`, `npm run check` and the 40 focused inverse-filter, codebook, Rust parity and engine-size tests pass. The current CI Rust job also passes 94 native unit tests, 120 parity/integration tests, seven thread tests, fmt/clippy, `no_std` and all three Wasm size checks.\\n\\nThe Wasm size ceiling rises to the next 16 KiB boundary, 294,912 bytes. Measured Rust 1.100.0 sizes after merging `main` through `1f016e0` (the articulatory codebook): scalar 278,782 bytes, SIMD 286,142 bytes; CI threads build 287,590 bytes. Both public APIs are preserved. Existing synthesis exports and ABI version remain compatible. A bounded Rust regression reproduced and verifies a fixed out-of-bounds panic when a supplied pitch leaves only one analysed harmonic: source H1-H2 is NaN, matching JS.\\n\\n[Final CI run 44039584980](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44039584980) passes on **`3c3152d8e1053ef9c8cf785b35abefa2b9ca8e90`**, including the Rust engine and all nine Node/Bun/Deno × Ubuntu/macOS/Windows jobs. The [dedicated Ubuntu Node CPU check](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44039584980/job/133891341226) measured **0.03577 RTF**, below the enforced 0.10 limit. All four companion workflows—Security, Workflows, Example app and Broken Link Checker—also pass on this exact SHA. Latest `main` is merged, the working tree is clean, and the PR is ready for review.\\n\\nThe companion [link-check job](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44035343515/job/133876788349) failed on an existing PTDB-TUG citation: the log records a timeout at line 225 and no recovery after retries at line 271. It identified the 2026-10-05 archived snapshot at line 292. The refusal registry, report generator and generated pitch report now cite that snapshot; licence decisions and measurements are unchanged. No check is disabled.\\n\",\"number\":141,\"title\":\"Add batch glottal inverse filtering and LF source measures (#61)\"}]\nExperimental landmark detector with unresolved quality gates (#62) true 190bde281044e5bf2abd3c7907ae180a88872cb5\n[\n  {\n    url: 'https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6946870187',\n    body: '## ❌ Auto-restart 5/5 - limit reached\\n' +\n      '\\n' +\n      '**Remaining blocker:** CI failures detected\\n' +\n      '\\n' +\n      'There were no uncommitted changes left to preserve.\\n' +\n      '\\n' +\n      'No more sessions will start automatically. Resolve the blocker, or rerun with a higher `--auto-restart-max-iterations`.'\n  },\n  {\n    url: 'https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6947242499',\n    body: 'We must find a way to make CI/CD fully green here, we should give realistic requirements and fully deliver them.\\r\\n' +\n      '\\r\\n' +\n      'The entire goal of pull request to be merged, not be permanent draft.'\n  },\n  {\n    url: 'https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6947269771',\n    body: '🤖 **AI Work Session Started**\\n' +\n      '\\n' +\n      'Started at 2026-11-17T11:53:04.123Z. Please wait for it to finish before giving feedback.\\n' +\n      '\\n' +\n      '_Runtime: solve `v2.39.10` · tool `codex` · model `gpt-6.1-sol` · task image `konard/hive-mind-dind:2.39.10@sha256:3be89e0510e606204a332e64547ebcfb4c8e527476abbbbbcdc7dac124476a86`_'\n  }\n]\n/** Syllable nuclei and acoustic landmarks (Mermelstein 1975, Liu 1996,\n * de Jong and Wempe 2009). Reads only the analysis frame set. */\nimport { createNucleusScanner } from './landmark-nuclei.js';\nimport { LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS } from './landmark-thresholds.js';\nimport {\n  BROAD_CLASSES,\n  sonorityFilters,\n  fillSonority,\n  smoothSonority,\n  landmarkCandidates,\n  classifyFrame,\n  cleanClasses,\n} from './landmark-signals.js';\nexport { BROAD_CLASSES };\n\nfunction thresholds(options) {\n  const T = { ...LANDMARK_THRESHOLDS, ...options.thresholds };\n  for (const [name, value] of Object.entries(T)) {\n    if (!Number.isFinite(value)) {\n      throw new RangeError(`threshold ${name} must be finite`);\n    }\n  }\n  if (T.voiced < 0 || T.voiced > 1 || T.nucleusDip < 0 || T.landmarkRise <= 0) {\n    throw new RangeError('invalid voicing, dip or rise threshold');\n  }\n  return T;\n}\n\nfunction previousLandmarks(output, first) {\n  const previous = new Map();\n  for (const item of output.landmarks) {\n    const t = Math.round((item.time - output.startTime) / output.hop);\n    if (t < first) {\n      previous.set(item.type, { t, type: item.type, strength: item.strength });\n    }\n  }\n  return [...previous.values()];\n}\n\n/**\n * A stage is invalid after trim/reset. `advance(true)` drains the final\n * lookahead, after the analyzer has been flushed. Returned nuclei are the\n * same objects appended to output.nuclei, and are never retracted.\n *\n * Closure clean-up is retrospective in batch mode. Streaming labels honour\n * the 60 ms commitment deadline; an open silence run is not relabelled after\n * commitment. Batch and streaming classes can consequently differ. Confirmed\n * nucleus times take priority over later higher peaks within 80 ms. See\n * docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md for the measured quality and timing contract.\n * @param {import('./frontend.js').FrameSet} frames\n * @param {import('./landmarks.js').LandmarkOptions} [options]\n */\nexport function createLandmarkDetector(frames, options = {}) {\n  if (\n    !(frames.hop > 0) ||\n    !Number.isInteger(frames.capacity) ||\n    frames.capacity < 0\n  ) {\n    throw new RangeError('invalid frame set');\n  }\n  const T = thresholds(options);\n  const filters = sonorityFilters(frames);\n  const raw = new Float32Array(frames.capacity);\n  const rawClasses = new Uint8Array(frames.capacity);\n  const output = {\n    hop: frames.hop,\n    startTime: frames.startTime,\n    count: 0,\n    committed: 0,\n    classes: new Uint8Array(frames.capacity),\n    sonority: new Float32Array(frames.capacity),\n    landmarks: [],\n    nuclei: [],\n  };\n  let seen = 0;\n  let finalized = false;\n  const radius = Math.round(0.04 / frames.hop);\n  const smoothing = Math.ceil(0.02 / frames.hop);\n  const landmarkDelay = Math.ceil(0.07 / frames.hop);\n  const time = (t) => output.startTime + t * frames.hop;\n  const s = output.sonority;\n  const scanNuclei = createNucleusScanner(frames, output, T);\n\n  function classifyPending(candidates) {\n    for (let t = output.committed; t < seen; t++) {\n      let peak = -Infinity;\n      for (\n        let j = Math.max(0, t - Math.round(0.2 / frames.hop));\n        j <= Math.min(seen - 1, t + radius);\n        j++\n      ) {\n        peak = Math.max(peak, s[j]);\n      }\n      const earlier = Math.max(0, t - Math.round(0.02 / frames.hop));\n      const burst =\n        (rawClasses[earlier] === 0 || rawClasses[earlier] === 6) &&\n        candidates.some(\n          (item) =>\n            item.type === 'b+' &&\n            item.t <= t &&\n            (t - item.t) * frames.hop <= 0.02 + 1e-9\n        );\n      rawClasses[t] = classifyFrame(frames, s, t, peak, burst, T);\n    }\n  }\n\n  return {\n    frames,\n    output,\n    advance(final = false) {\n      if (frames.startTime !== output.startTime || frames.count < seen) {\n        throw new Error('landmark stage invalid after trim/reset');\n      }\n      if (finalized) {\n        if (frames.count !== seen) {\n          throw new Error('advance after final');\n        }\n        return [];\n      }\n      if (frames.count > frames.capacity) {\n        throw new RangeError('frame count exceeds capacity');\n      }\n      fillSonority(frames, raw, seen, filters);\n      smoothSonority(\n        raw,\n        s,\n        Math.max(0, seen - smoothing),\n        frames.count,\n        frames.hop\n      );\n      seen = frames.count;\n      output.count = seen;\n      const emitted = [];\n      const stable = final ? seen : Math.max(0, seen - smoothing - radius);\n      scanNuclei(stable, emitted, final);\n      const priorTime = output.landmarks.at(-1)?.time ?? -Infinity;\n      const first = Math.max(\n        0,\n        Math.floor((priorTime - output.startTime) / frames.hop) -\n          Math.round(0.02 / frames.hop)\n      );\n      const candidates = landmarkCandidates(\n        frames,\n        T.landmarkRise,\n        first,\n        seen,\n        previousLandmarks(output, first)\n      );\n      const last = final ? seen : Math.max(0, seen - landmarkDelay);\n      for (const item of candidates) {\n        if (item.t < last && time(item.t) > priorTime + 1e-9) {\n          output.landmarks.push({\n            time: time(item.t),\n            type: item.type,\n            strength: item.strength,\n          });\n        }\n      }\n      classifyPending(candidates);\n      const cleaned = cleanClasses(rawClasses, seen, frames.hop);\n      output.classes.set(cleaned.subarray(output.committed), output.committed);\n      output.committed = final\n        ? seen\n        : Math.max(0, seen - Math.ceil(0.06 / frames.hop));\n      finalized = final;\n      return emitted;\n    },\n  };\n}\n\n/** Whole-recording version of the same stage. */\nexport function findLandmarks(frames, options = {}) {\n  const detector = createLandmarkDetector(frames, options);\n  detector.advance(true);\n  return detector.output;\n}\nimport type { FrameSet } from './frontend.js';\nexport type BroadClass =\n  | 'silence'\n  | 'vowel'\n  | 'glide'\n  | 'nasal'\n  | 'voiced-fricative'\n  | 'voiceless-fricative'\n  | 'closure'\n  | 'burst';\nexport declare const BROAD_CLASSES: readonly BroadClass[];\nexport interface LandmarkThresholds {\n  silence: number;\n  voiced: number;\n  fricativeZcr: number;\n  fricativeGravity: number;\n  nasalDrop: number;\n  nasalBelowPeak: number;\n  glideBelowPeak: number;\n  nucleusAboveNoise: number;\n  nucleusDip: number;\n  landmarkRise: number;\n}\nexport interface LandmarkOptions {\n  thresholds?: Partial<LandmarkThresholds>;\n}\nexport interface Nucleus {\n  /** Immutable once confirmed; later higher peaks within 80 ms are ignored. */\n  time: number;\n  start: number;\n  /** Unknown until a following minimum or nonspeech frame arrives. */\n  end: number | null;\n  strength: number;\n}\nexport interface Landmark {\n  time: number;\n  type: 'g+' | 'g-' | 's+' | 's-' | 'b+' | 'b-';\n  strength: number;\n}\nexport interface LandmarkResult {\n  hop: number;\n  startTime: number;\n  count: number;\n  /** Immutable class prefix: count minus 60 ms of frames, or count at final.\n   * Streaming preserves this prefix even when batch would relabel a closure. */\n  committed: number;\n  /** Broad acoustic guesses; see the documented experimental accuracy. */\n  classes: Uint8Array;\n  sonority: Float32Array;\n  landmarks: Landmark[];\n  nuclei: Nucleus[];\n}\nexport interface LandmarkDetector {\n  readonly frames: FrameSet;\n  readonly output: LandmarkResult;\n  /** Confirmed nuclei appended by this call; final drains the lookahead. */\n  advance(final?: boolean): Nucleus[];\n}\nexport declare function findLandmarks(\n  frames: FrameSet,\n  options?: LandmarkOptions\n): LandmarkResult;\nexport declare function createLandmarkDetector(\n  frames: FrameSet,\n  options?: LandmarkOptions\n): LandmarkDetector;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
