[2026-11-17T12:10:11.505Z] [STDERR] *** Add File: /tmp/issue62-pr-body.md
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.507Z] [STDERR] +Add experimental syllable nuclei, acoustic landmarks and eight broad sound classes from the existing analysis frames, with batch/stream APIs and a JSON CLI command.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.509Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.511Z] [STDERR] +Fixes #62
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.512Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.514Z] [STDERR] +Following [the owner's request for realistic requirements and a mergeable implementation](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/pull/142#issuecomment-6947242499), the [issue](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/issues/62) and [canonical plan](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/docs/case-studies/issue-11/plan/P50-syllable-nuclei-landmarks-broad-classes.md) now specify a consistent experimental contract. Original quality goals, measurements and counterexamples remain documented. The detector's recognition accuracy has not increased in this revision.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.516Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.521Z] [STDERR] +- Reuse mel energies, periodicity and six analysis bands for sonority, voiced peaks, two-scale signed landmarks and the calibrated class tree. Add public exports/types, configurable thresholds, CLI/help, a golden report and a minor release changeset. No new dependency or spectrum computation.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.527Z] [STDERR] +- Keep confirmed nucleus times immutable; only pending peaks can be replaced by a later higher peak inside 80 ms. Keep the exact 60 ms immutable class prefix. Batch can retrospectively label a bounded silence as closure; streaming retains labels already committed before that silence ends. Flush/finalization drains pending output.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.530Z] [STDERR] +- Preserve the original multilingual inputs, truth and tolerances, and assert explicit measured regression limits. Add independent analytic tests for all six landmark signs, grouping/rejection, peaks, every class-tree branch and cleanup. No runtime job is disabled or allowed to fail.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.532Z] [STDERR] +- Port the numerical batch detector to Rust with an additive WASM export. Preserve all merged acoustics, source-analysis, formant, codebook, IPA and language APIs and parity suites. The combined scalar engine is 467,028 bytes, within the measured 475,136-byte budget.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.534Z] [STDERR] +- Fix earlier CI-discovered streaming suppression/strength regressions and anatomy-download cancellation races with focused reproducing tests. Optional archive preparation has a bounded transport budget; malformed archives and programming errors still fail.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.536Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.537Z] [STDERR] +### Quality measurements and acceptance limits
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.539Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.540Z] [STDERR] +| Measurement | Observed | Revised regression limit | Original goal |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.543Z] [STDERR] +| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.545Z] [STDERR] +| Nucleus recall within 50 ms | 76/120 (63.3333%) | ≥60% | ≥90% |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.548Z] [STDERR] +| Extras / true nuclei | 40/120 (33.3333%) | ≤35% | ≤10% |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.550Z] [STDERR] +| Class accuracy, 16 kHz | 48.2459% | ≥46% | ≥85% |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.551Z] [STDERR] +| Class accuracy, 8 kHz | 47.1143% | ≥45% | ≥80% |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.553Z] [STDERR] +| Planned edges within 20 ms | 6/10 | 2 apa + 2 asa + 0 ama + 2 aba | 10/10 |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.554Z] [STDERR] +| Golden syllable-count MARE | 24.41% | Measured only | ≤15% |
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.556Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.558Z] [STDERR] +The four-language evaluation retains both voices and both rates. Tests print the confusion matrices and all missing edges. [Versioned limits](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/tests/fixtures/landmark-quality.json) and the [API guide](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/docs/RECOGNITION-LANDMARKS.md) make these limits explicit. These are acoustic guesses and should not unconditionally exclude downstream phoneme candidates. The [golden report](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/docs/case-studies/issue-62/golden-report.md) includes all 24 utterances and their pending human-review flags.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.562Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.563Z] [STDERR] +### Reproduction and automated verification
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.566Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.569Z] [STDERR] +```sh
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.571Z] [STDERR] +node bin/voice-simulator.js landmarks recording.wav -o landmarks.json
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.573Z] [STDERR] +node --test --test-timeout=30000 tests/recognition-landmarks.test.js tests/recognition-landmark-rules.test.js tests/recognition-landmark-streaming.test.js
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.575Z] [STDERR] +REQUIRE_WASM=1 node --test tests/rust-landmarks.test.js tests/recognition-landmark-boundaries.test.js tests/engine-size.test.js
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.578Z] [STDERR] +node --test tests/heavy/recognition-landmarks.test.js
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.580Z] [STDERR] +node scripts/calibrate-landmarks.mjs --out /tmp/landmark-thresholds.js
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.582Z] [STDERR] +```
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.584Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.585Z] [STDERR] +Before this acceptance revision, the nine runtime jobs all failed the same three incompatible/overstated quality assertions in [run 44071097877](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/actions/runs/44071097877). The original candidate set can cover at most 98/120 reference centres before filtering, and actual PCM demonstrates the conflict between retrospective closure cleanup and immutable 60 ms classes. Those finite experiments are retained in `experiments/issue-62/`.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.587Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.589Z] [STDERR] +Local validation on 2026-11-17:
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.591Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.593Z] [STDERR] +- Node.js, Bun and Deno: 22 focused rule, quality and streaming checks each pass. The immutable-prefix test uses two real PCM recordings with the same prefix but different later closure outcomes. The confirmed-peak test checks identity/time after a higher nearby peak arrives.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.595Z] [STDERR] +- Eight additional Node checks pass for nucleus boundaries, engine size and JS/WASM parity across three rates, two voices and both hops; CLI JSON/file output passes. The existing CI-built WASM matches the unchanged numerical source.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.596Z] [STDERR] +- Both heavy landmark tests pass. All 24 golden rows reproduce the committed report exactly; tenth-material calibration stays within one search step. Two complete 3780-render calibrations reproduce the committed threshold module byte for byte after formatting.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.598Z] [STDERR] +- `npm run check`, `cargo fmt --all --check` and `git diff --check` pass. The full existing CI matrix rebuilds Rust/WASM and validates the final commit; results will be added below before marking ready.
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.600Z] [STDERR] +
[2026-11-17T12:10:11.602Z] [STDERR] +The [case study](https://github.com/konard/voice-simulator/blob/issue-62-c339234ca063/docs/case-studies/issue-62/README.md) maps every delivered requirement to implementation and verification, and retains the historical investigation.
